  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DVjRQVLDbAw/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>Everything is a win when the goal is experience.</b>”\n— isabelradford_\n\n<i>Fear of wrong decisions and comparison with others causes stress, but reframing success as experience over perfection eliminates regret.</i>\n💡 <b>You only see others&#x27; highlights; focus on your own learning and growth rather than being right or perfect.</b>\n\n💾 <i>Reframes perfectionism and comparison anxiety into a permission structure for authentic living and growth.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DVjRQVLDbAw/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#mindset #perspective #experience</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>Everything is a win when the goal is experience.</b>”<br>— isabelradford_<br><i>Fear of wrong decisions and comparison with others causes stress, but reframing success as experience over perfection eliminates regret.</i><br>💡 <b>You only see others&#x27; highlights; focus on your own learning and growth rather than being right or perfect.</b><br>💾 <i>Reframes perfectionism and comparison anxiety into a permission structure for authentic living and growth.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DVjRQVLDbAw/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#mindset #perspective #experience</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>At 24, fear of wrong decisions drives constant career and love discussions. The reframing: goal is experience, not perfection. You see all your flaws; others show only highlights. Nothing is wasted when the metric is learning.\n\nI recently read this Substack article titled Everything is a win when the goal is experience. Now it really got me thinking because I&#x27;m 24 and I&#x27;ve noticed the two main topics of conversation with my friends is careers and love. Now I think the frequency of these discussions comes from a fear, a fear of making the wrong decision and living with regret. Comparing ourselves with what other people are doing, whether they&#x27;re making more money or they&#x27;re in the perfect relationship, which more often or not makes you feel behind or dissatisfied or stressed out. But this article reframed everything for me because the goal isn&#x27;t about doing things right or doing things perfectly. The goal is experience. And that means getting things wrong, trying things and growing away from them or pursuing something new. And remember that you only see other people&#x27;s highlights and what they&#x27;re willing to share with you. Whereas for yourself, you know everything about you. So you see all your flaws and mistakes. It&#x27;s not comparable. When you look at life with this goal, nothing is wasted and only you get to decide what is regret and what is simply learning and living.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-16T19:28:01"
  },
