  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DY4lf4MIpfo/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "🎬 Relocating to a new country strips away safety nets, social roles, and comfort — forcing the self-examination that every wealthy, successful person had to go through. Distance builds people; comfort doesn&#x27;t.\n🏷 Mindset · Quote\n📄 <i>Everytime I moved to a new country… my life changed in ways I can&#x27;t even describe. MOVE, LEARN, ADAPT &amp; do it all over again every couple years.</i>\n\n💬 <b>QUOTE</b>\n• <b>“comfort never made anything and anybody great but distance did”</b> — Afnan Khalifa (@theafnankhalifa)\n   ↳ Clean hook line — use verbatim as a reel/thread caption. Your Dagestan→SF→Dubai→SF arc is the lived proof; this quote frames the whole story.\n\n💡 <b>ADVICE</b>\n• When you land somewhere with no safety net and no one who knows your story, the silence forces you to ask what you actually want — that&#x27;s the same fire every successful person walked through\n   ↳ Your own relocation story is this reel. Use the before/after frame — who you were vs. who you became — as explicit content for your athlete platform audience, many of whom are immigrants or expats. Related vault note: context-about-me.md.\n• List what you were tolerating back home that you only noticed after you left — because everyone around you was tolerating the same thing\n   ↳ Actionable reflection exercise. Run this against your current environment and log findings in GAMEPLAN — it&#x27;s a recurring audit, not a one-time insight. Vault note: Everything is a win when the goal is experience.md covers this exact reframe.\n\n📝 Action Inbox/2026-06-13 moving countries makes you rich.md · 🗂 Notion: 1 reel · 3 items",
    "markdown": "# Moving countries makes you rich\n\n*🏷 Mindset · Quote*\n\nRelocating to a new country strips away safety nets, social roles, and comfort — forcing the self-examination that every wealthy, successful person had to go through. Distance builds people; comfort doesn't.\n\n> Everytime I moved to a new country… my life changed in ways I can't even describe. MOVE, LEARN, ADAPT & do it all over again every couple years.\n\n---\n\n### 💬 Quote\n> **“comfort never made anything and anybody great but distance did”** — Afnan Khalifa (@theafnankhalifa)\n> Clean hook line — use verbatim as a reel/thread caption. Your Dagestan→SF→Dubai→SF arc is the lived proof; this quote frames the whole story.\n\n### 💡 Advice\n- When you land somewhere with no safety net and no one who knows your story, the silence forces you to ask what you actually want — that's the same fire every successful person walked through — Your own relocation story is this reel. Use the before/after frame — who you were vs. who you became — as explicit content for your athlete platform audience, many of whom are immigrants or expats. Related vault note: context-about-me.md.\n- List what you were tolerating back home that you only noticed after you left — because everyone around you was tolerating the same thing — Actionable reflection exercise. Run this against your current environment and log findings in GAMEPLAN — it's a recurring audit, not a one-time insight. Vault note: Everything is a win when the goal is experience.md covers this exact reframe.\n\n---\n\n*📝 Action Inbox/2026-06-13 moving countries makes you rich.md · 🗂 Notion: 1 reel · 3 items*",
