  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYpx5RwIqBW/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "🎬 8-step framework for building a personal brand as a fictional protagonist: mission, character, ability, weakness, allies, enemy, mentor, rival — ends with a reshare challenge.\n🏷 Mindset\n📄 <i>Mission: To become the most valuable creative director on planet earth\n\nCharacter: a silly but passionate and relentless family man.\n\nAbility: Creative Writing, Ideation, obsessed with learning\n\nWeakness: Organisation, Numbers and Sense of Direction</i>\n\n🛠 <b>TRY</b>\n• <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYpx5RwIqBW/\">Film a &#x27;main character brand sheet&#x27; reel: declare your mission, character, ability, weakness, allies, enemy, mentor, and rival on camera</a>\n   ↳ Creator offers to reshare every person who completes this challenge on his story — direct audience growth play for Magomed&#x27;s IG with zero ad spend; also forces clarity on his own positioning.\n\n💡 <b>ADVICE</b>\n• Your mission must be non-monetary and so big it scares you — hitting a number goal ends in depression; only an open-ended identity-level mission sustains you.\n   ↳ Magomed is building an athlete platform and a personal brand simultaneously — framing both around a single audacious mission (not a revenue target) will make his content more magnetic and keep him motivated past early milestones.\n• Name your enemy publicly and be vocal about it — the villain role creates narrative tension, filters your audience, and makes your positioning instantly clear.\n   ↳ Magomed competes in a crowded content/athlete space; declaring what he is against (e.g., surface-level fitness influencers vs. serious athlete development) would sharpen his brand and attract the right followers.\n• Share your weaknesses explicitly on camera — the most likeable creators reveal their flaws, not just their strengths.\n   ↳ As a founder-creator, projecting only wins risks coming across as inaccessible; openly naming weak spots (e.g., ops, sales) builds trust with his audience of athletes and potential partners.\n\n📝 Action Inbox/2026-06-13 main-character-personal-brand-8-steps.md · 🗂 Notion: 1 reel · 4 items",
    "markdown": "# 8-step main character brand framework\n\n*🏷 Mindset*\n\n8-step framework for building a personal brand as a fictional protagonist: mission, character, ability, weakness, allies, enemy, mentor, rival — ends with a reshare challenge.\n\n> Mission: To become the most valuable creative director on planet earth\n\nCharacter: a silly but passionate and relentless family man.\n\nAbility: Creative Writing, Ideation, obsessed with learning\n\nWeakness: Organisation, Numbers and Sense of Direction\n\n---\n\n### 🛠 Try\n- [Film a 'main character brand sheet' reel: declare your mission, character, ability, weakness, allies, enemy, mentor, and rival on camera](https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYpx5RwIqBW/) — Creator offers to reshare every person who completes this challenge on his story — direct audience growth play for Magomed's IG with zero ad spend; also forces clarity on his own positioning.\n\n### 💡 Advice\n- Your mission must be non-monetary and so big it scares you — hitting a number goal ends in depression; only an open-ended identity-level mission sustains you. — Magomed is building an athlete platform and a personal brand simultaneously — framing both around a single audacious mission (not a revenue target) will make his content more magnetic and keep him motivated past early milestones.\n- Name your enemy publicly and be vocal about it — the villain role creates narrative tension, filters your audience, and makes your positioning instantly clear. — Magomed competes in a crowded content/athlete space; declaring what he is against (e.g., surface-level fitness influencers vs. serious athlete development) would sharpen his brand and attract the right followers.\n- Share your weaknesses explicitly on camera — the most likeable creators reveal their flaws, not just their strengths. — As a founder-creator, projecting only wins risks coming across as inaccessible; openly naming weak spots (e.g., ops, sales) builds trust with his audience of athletes and potential partners.\n\n---\n\n*📝 Action Inbox/2026-06-13 main-character-personal-brand-8-steps.md · 🗂 Notion: 1 reel · 4 items*",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-13T19:58:02"
