    "digest": "<b>🎬 Four Books on AI and Craft</b>\n🏷 <i>Recommendations</i>\nShort talking-head reel by @meshtimes recommending four books spanning AI and creativity, algorithmic music, the power behind OpenAI, and software craftsmanship.\n<blockquote>The creator lists four books worth reading: Creative Machines (AI and human creativity), Mood Machine (Spotify&#x27;s algorithmic influence on taste), Empire of AI (the people and power driving OpenAI), and Apprenticeship Patterns (practical skill-building for software developers).</blockquote>\n<b>📚 Read</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Creative-Machines-Future-Human-Creativity/dp/1394316267\">Creative Machines: AI, Art &amp; Us</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; subtitle is AI, Art &amp; Us; hardcover and Kindle available)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Mood-Machine-Spotify-Perfect-Playlist/dp/1668083515\">Mood Machine: The Rise of Spotify and the Costs of the Perfect Playlist</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; National Bestseller, NBCC John Leonard Prize finalist)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Empire-AI-Dreams-Nightmares-Altmans/dp/0593657500\">Empire of AI: Dreams and Nightmares in Sam Altman&#x27;s OpenAI</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; NYT Bestseller and NBCC Award for Nonfiction winner)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Apprenticeship-Patterns-Guidance-Aspiring-Craftsman/dp/0596518382\">Apprenticeship Patterns: Guidance for the Aspiring Software Craftsman</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon and Goodreads; published 2009, rated 4.10 on Goodreads)</i>\n<i>📝 Action Inbox/2026-06-14 Four Books on AI and Craft.md · 🗂 Notion: 1 reel · 4 items</i>",
