    "digest": "<b>🎬 5 Books Every AI Engineer Must Read</b>\n🏷 <i>Recommendations · Tools &amp; AI</i>\nShort-form vertical reel rapidly listing 5 must-read books for AI engineers in 2026, with titles shown on screen in succession over ~7 seconds.\n<blockquote>The creator lists 5 books recommended for AI engineers: Building LLMs for Production, AI Engineering (Chip Huyen), Context Engineering for Multi-Agent Systems (Denis Rothman), Designing Machine Learning Systems (Chip Huyen), and LLM Engineer&#x27;s Handbook (Iusztin &amp; Labonne).</blockquote>\n<b>📚 Read</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Building-LLMs-Production-Reliability-Fine-Tuning/dp/B0D4FFPFW8\">Building LLMs for Production</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; 470-page guide covering prompting, fine-tuning, RAG, agents, deployment)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/AI-Engineering-Building-Applications-Foundation/dp/1098166302\">AI Engineering: Building Applications with Foundation Models</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; published January 2025, most-read book on O&#x27;Reilly platform)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Context-Engineering-Multi-Agent-Systems-architecture/dp/1806690055\">Context Engineering for Multi-Agent Systems</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon and Packt; covers Context Engine design, MCP, memory, multi-agent coordination)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Designing-Machine-Learning-Systems-Production-Ready/dp/1098107969\">Designing Machine Learning Systems</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; O&#x27;Reilly 2022, covers iterative framework for production ML systems)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/LLM-Engineers-Handbook-engineering-production/dp/1836200072\">LLM Engineer&#x27;s Handbook</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon and Packt; end-to-end LLM product development including fine-tuning, RAG, deployment)</i>\n<i>📝 Action Inbox/2026-06-14 5 Books Every AI Engineer Must Read.md · 🗂 Notion: 1 reel · 5 items</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>🎬 5 Books Every AI Engineer Must Read</b>\n🏷 <i>Recommendations · Tools &amp; AI</i>\nShort-form vertical reel rapidly listing 5 must-read books for AI engineers in 2026, with titles shown on screen in succession over ~7 seconds.\n<blockquote>The creator lists 5 books recommended for AI engineers: Building LLMs for Production, AI Engineering (Chip Huyen), Context Engineering for Multi-Agent Systems (Denis Rothman), Designing Machine Learning Systems (Chip Huyen), and LLM Engineer&#x27;s Handbook (Iusztin &amp; Labonne).</blockquote>\n<b>📚 Read</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Building-LLMs-Production-Reliability-Fine-Tuning/dp/B0D4FFPFW8\">Building LLMs for Production</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; 470-page guide covering prompting, fine-tuning, RAG, agents, deployment)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/AI-Engineering-Building-Applications-Foundation/dp/1098166302\">AI Engineering: Building Applications with Foundation Models</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; published January 2025, most-read book on O&#x27;Reilly platform)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Context-Engineering-Multi-Agent-Systems-architecture/dp/1806690055\">Context Engineering for Multi-Agent Systems</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon and Packt; covers Context Engine design, MCP, memory, multi-agent coordination)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Designing-Machine-Learning-Systems-Production-Ready/dp/1098107969\">Designing Machine Learning Systems</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon; O&#x27;Reilly 2022, covers iterative framework for production ML systems)</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/LLM-Engineers-Handbook-engineering-production/dp/1836200072\">LLM Engineer&#x27;s Handbook</a> <i>(confirmed on Amazon and Packt; end-to-end LLM product development including fine-tuning, RAG, deployment)</i>\n<i>📝 Action Inbox/2026-06-14 5 Books Every AI Engineer Must Read.md · 🗂 Notion: 1 reel · 5 items</i>",
