  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZhUcdRN4EF/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>5 Free Games That Build Intelligence</b>\n<i>“the most underrated way of getting smarter is simply by playing games”</i>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://anthropeum.com/\">Anthropeum</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://timeguessr.com/\">TimeGuessr</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://wikitrivia.tomjwatson.com/\">Wikitrivia</a> — Tom J. Watson\n✅ <a href=\"https://sudoku.com/\">Sudoku</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.puzzle-nonograms.com/\">Nonograms</a>\n\n💾 <i>A vetted list of five free browser games, each targeting a distinct cognitive skill, backed by neuroscience framing from the caption.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZhUcdRN4EF/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#games #reasoning #learning</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>5 Free Games That Build Intelligence</b>\n<i>“the most underrated way of getting smarter is simply by playing games”</i>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://anthropeum.com/\">Anthropeum</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://timeguessr.com/\">TimeGuessr</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://wikitrivia.tomjwatson.com/\">Wikitrivia</a> — Tom J. Watson\n✅ <a href=\"https://sudoku.com/\">Sudoku</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.puzzle-nonograms.com/\">Nonograms</a>\n\n💾 <i>A vetted list of five free browser games, each targeting a distinct cognitive skill, backed by neuroscience framing from the caption.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZhUcdRN4EF/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#games #reasoning #learning</i>\n<details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Part 2 of a games guide for cognitive improvement. Anthropeum trains cultural geography and temporal reasoning; TimeGuessr trains historical and geographic pattern recognition; Wikitrivia trains chronological sequencing of world events; Sudoku isolates working memory and logical inference; Nonograms build spatial and deductive reasoning through picture-reveal grid puzzles.\n\nthe most underrated way of getting smarter is simply by playing games so this is part two of the nerdy girl guide to the best games on the internet first up i have only just discovered this recently and it&#x27;s called anthropium you&#x27;re given 10 objects for the metropolitan museum&#x27;s collection and you have to guess where those objects were made and when it&#x27;s training both your geographic and your temporal reasoning and it&#x27;s giving you a material sense of culture that a lot of people feel like people are losing nowadays really similar to this time guesser shows you a historical photograph you have to guess what the year is and where on the globe it was taken so a bit like geo guesser you start to learn how to identify different characteristics of different countries and it&#x27;s a really just fun way of building an understanding of the world one that i have been playing for a while is wiki trivia you get a set of people and events from history and you have to place them in a timeline in the correct order now i find this super brilliant because it&#x27;s training your ability to understand what was going on in different parts of the world at the same time like i always find it very crazy that for example oxford and cambridge university are older than the aztec and the incan empires you might think that this is really obvious but i would be so remiss to not mention sudoku you fill a nine by nine grid so every row column and three by three box has the digits one to nine once and sudoku is actually one of the best ways of isolating your working memory and training your logical inference while you might have heard of sudoku you probably haven&#x27;t heard of nonograms and this is when each row column tells you how many cells in that row column is filled and you have to try and figure out which of those cells are filled and when you do that it builds up a picture there&#x27;s this added spatial and visual element and again everything can be revealed through deductive reasoning which is one of the most important skills to be training at the moment follow along if you want to part three</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-14T21:15:22"
  },
  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYdRDXdOWvO/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>4 Print Papers to Cut Screen Time</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.goodgoodgood.co/goodnewspaper\">Goodnewspaper (Good Good Good)</a> — Good Good Good\n✅ <a href=\"https://sundayclub.com\">Sunday Club</a> — Black King Games\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.thekindnesscompany.com/collections/history-nation\">History Nation</a> — The Kindness Company\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.bookmarksmagazine.com\">Bookmarks Magazine</a> — Bookmarks Magazine\n\n💾 <i>Curates four distinct print publications — good news, puzzles, history, and book reviews — as concrete, verified screen-free reading alternatives.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYdRDXdOWvO/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#print #screen-time #newspapers</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>4 Print Papers to Cut Screen Time</b><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.goodgoodgood.co/goodnewspaper\">Goodnewspaper (Good Good Good)</a> — Good Good Good</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://sundayclub.com\">Sunday Club</a> — Black King Games</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.thekindnesscompany.com/collections/history-nation\">History Nation</a> — The Kindness Company</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.bookmarksmagazine.com\">Bookmarks Magazine</a> — Bookmarks Magazine</li></ol><br>💾 <i>Curates four distinct print publications — good news, puzzles, history, and book reviews — as concrete, verified screen-free reading alternatives.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYdRDXdOWvO/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#print #screen-time #newspapers</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>A roundup of four print publications: Goodnewspaper (positive world news, monthly), Sunday Club (original puzzles, quarterly), History Nation (historical stories, monthly), and Bookmarks Magazine (aggregated book reviews, bi-monthly) — all as alternatives to scrolling.\n\ncool newspapers for people who want to lower their screen time number one good good good newspaper this is a monthly print about good stories that are happening all around the world it was kind of made to counteract all of the really bad news we hear all the time all they do is share great news happening about people volunteering or good things happening in politics politics they&#x27;re bright it&#x27;s colorful number two the sunday club this is a quarterly newspaper that&#x27;s focused on pushing out puzzles any puzzle you can think of they drop it in like six pages it&#x27;s awesome i&#x27;m doing puzzles i&#x27;ve never even heard of this would be really good for people who like wortel and want more of wortel number three history nation this is a monthly newspaper that focuses on publishing historical stories it&#x27;s your classic history class but in newspaper form you can read about conquests about interesting artifacts number four bookmarks bookmarks is a bi-monthly magazine that is made by book lovers for book lovers essentially their team reads 500 books and then does little mini reviews of them so this is a great way to find new books that isn&#x27;t on tick tock reddit goodreads etc etc i rest my case</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-15T00:33:21"
  },
