    "digest": "<b>4 Free YouTubers to Learn ML</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCDklgnaowWTNnL2y8V_nAEA\">Andrej Karpathy</a> — Andrej Karpathy\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfzlCWGWYyIQ0aLC5w48gBQ\">Sentdex</a> — Harrison Kinsley\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/3blue1brown\">3Blue1Brown</a> — Grant Sanderson\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtYLUTtgS3k1Fg4y5tAhLbw\">StatQuest with Josh Starmer</a> — Josh Starmer\n\n💾 <i>A vetted, free starter stack covering ML theory, math intuition, and practical coding across four complementary YouTube channels.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DV94u8fDI3l/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#machine-learning #youtube #education</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>4 Free YouTubers to Learn ML</b><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCDklgnaowWTNnL2y8V_nAEA\">Andrej Karpathy</a> — Andrej Karpathy</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfzlCWGWYyIQ0aLC5w48gBQ\">Sentdex</a> — Harrison Kinsley</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/3blue1brown\">3Blue1Brown</a> — Grant Sanderson</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCtYLUTtgS3k1Fg4y5tAhLbw\">StatQuest with Josh Starmer</a> — Josh Starmer</li></ol><br>💾 <i>A vetted, free starter stack covering ML theory, math intuition, and practical coding across four complementary YouTube channels.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DV94u8fDI3l/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#machine-learning #youtube #education</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Four free YouTube channels covering ML from different angles — conceptual depth (Karpathy), practical coding (Sentdex), visual math (3Blue1Brown), and simplified statistics (StatQuest).\n\nMachine learning is way easier than you think, especially with these YouTubers. First, Adrash Kapathy. If you&#x27;re serious about understanding ML at a deep level, this man is the one. He doesn&#x27;t just teach you what to do, he teaches you why it works. Then, Scentdex. Super practical, get straight to the point. If you want to just start building things and figure it out as you go, start here. The classic three blue, one brown for the math side. I know math sounds scary, but the way he visualizes everything makes it feel way less math and more like art. Neural Networks finally made sense after I watched him. And StatQuest with Josh Starmer. Anytime I hit a concept and I don&#x27;t understand it, I go straight to him. He breaks down things so simply, it almost feels too easy. All these guys are free, comment YouTuber and I&#x27;ll send them to you.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
