  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi_McJtBWY/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>10 Habits to Stay Dangerously Overeducated</b>\n<i>A set of progressively niche learning habits designed to sharpen how you acquire, process, and connect knowledge.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Spend an hour a week debating someone smarter than you — debate to get taken apart, not to win.\n• Watch a lecture outside your field, then explain it from scratch.\n• Put on an educational video (politics, history, anything) while you eat instead of scrolling.\n• Explain every idea out loud until you hear where it breaks.\n• Keep a running list of things you don&#x27;t understand yet.\n• Read the original instead of someone&#x27;s summary of it.\n• Force two unrelated subjects to connect.\n• Get so good at processing information that an ordinary conversation can&#x27;t hold you anymore.\n\n💾 <i>Concrete, uncommon learning habits that go beyond generic &#x27;read more&#x27; advice — useful as a recurring personal audit.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi_McJtBWY/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#learning #education #habits</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>10 Habits to Stay Dangerously Overeducated</b><br><i>A set of progressively niche learning habits designed to sharpen how you acquire, process, and connect knowledge.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Spend an hour a week debating someone smarter than you — debate to get taken apart, not to win.</li><li>Watch a lecture outside your field, then explain it from scratch.</li><li>Put on an educational video (politics, history, anything) while you eat instead of scrolling.</li><li>Explain every idea out loud until you hear where it breaks.</li><li>Keep a running list of things you don&#x27;t understand yet.</li><li>Read the original instead of someone&#x27;s summary of it.</li><li>Force two unrelated subjects to connect.</li><li>Get so good at processing information that an ordinary conversation can&#x27;t hold you anymore.</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Concrete, uncommon learning habits that go beyond generic &#x27;read more&#x27; advice — useful as a recurring personal audit.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZi_McJtBWY/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#learning #education #habits</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Eight actionable habits for serious self-education: seek out smarter opponents to debate, cross fields deliberately, consume educational content passively, explain ideas aloud until they break, track ignorance, read originals, connect unrelated domains, and aim to outgrow ordinary conversation.\n\n10 out of 10 habits to become dangerously overeducated, but they get progressively more niche. Spend an hour a week debating someone smarter than you. And don&#x27;t debate to win, debate to get taken apart. Watch a lecture outside your field and then explain it from scratch. Put on an educational video, it can be about politics or history or whatever you want while you eat instead of scrolling. Explain every idea out loud until you hear where it breaks. Keep a running list of things you don&#x27;t understand yet. Read the original instead of someone&#x27;s summary of it. Force two subjects that have nothing to do with each other to connect. And get so good at processing information that an ordinary conversation can&#x27;t hold you anymore.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-15T14:13:08"
  },
  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DWBfwR6ik-0/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Library Architecture Shapes Your Brain</b>\n<i>Libraries are one of the most deliberately designed behavioral environments humans have created, using architecture to prime visitors for focused, expansive thought before they even open a book.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Behavioral affordance: a space signals to your brain what kind of behavior it expects from you.\n• High ceilings correlate with abstract thinking — studies show people in high-ceiling rooms perform better on tasks requiring creative or expansive thought.\n• Acoustic materials (carpet, wooden shelves) enforce quiet not through rules but through physics, telling your brain to slow down and focus.\n• Diffused or north-facing light — steady and even, without glare — relaxes the eyes and deepens attention.\n• Every element conspires to make you a more focused, intellectually ambitious version of yourself.\n\n💾 <i>Concise, research-backed explanation of how intentional architectural design shapes cognition and behavior through environmental psychology.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DWBfwR6ik-0/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#architecture #focus #behavioral-design</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Library Architecture Shapes Your Brain</b><br><i>Libraries are one of the most deliberately designed behavioral environments humans have created, using architecture to prime visitors for focused, expansive thought before they even open a book.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Behavioral affordance: a space signals to your brain what kind of behavior it expects from you.</li><li>High ceilings correlate with abstract thinking — studies show people in high-ceiling rooms perform better on tasks requiring creative or expansive thought.</li><li>Acoustic materials (carpet, wooden shelves) enforce quiet not through rules but through physics, telling your brain to slow down and focus.</li><li>Diffused or north-facing light — steady and even, without glare — relaxes the eyes and deepens attention.</li><li>Every element conspires to make you a more focused, intellectually ambitious version of yourself.</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Concise, research-backed explanation of how intentional architectural design shapes cognition and behavior through environmental psychology.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DWBfwR6ik-0/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#architecture #focus #behavioral-design</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Libraries are deliberately engineered behavioral environments. High ceilings encourage abstract thinking, acoustic materials calm the nervous system, and diffused light eases visual attention. The reel frames this through the lens of environmental psychology, calling it intentional behavioral design.\n\nYou walk into a library and immediately feel like you should be working on something important. That is not an accident. That is architecture doing its job. There is a concept in environmental psychology called the behavioral affordance. It basically means that a space signals to you what kind of behavior it expects. And libraries are one of the most deliberately designed behavioral environments humans have ever created. Start with the ceiling. Most great libraries have high ones. Not just for grandeur, though that&#x27;s part of it. High ceilings correlate with abstract thinking. Studies have found that people in high ceiling rooms perform better on darts that require creative or expansive thought. They literally think bigger. And then there is the silence. Library is enforced quiet, not just through rules, but through materials. Carpet absorbs sound. Wooden shelves diffuse it. The artistic environment tells your brain, slow, focus. This is a place for thought. And the light. Reading rooms almost always have north-facing or diffused light. Steady, even, without harsh shadows or glare. Your eyes relax and your attention deep. Every single element is conspiring you to be more focused, more intellectually ambitious version of yourself. The building wants something from you. And you walk out feeling like you gave it. That is the power of intentional design.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-15T14:13:39"
  },
  "https://www.instagram.com/p/DZmhWrXiBxU/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Казахстан: $10 млрд AI-сделка с NVIDIA</b>\n<i>Казахстан, Firebird и NVIDIA подписали пакет соглашений на $10 млрд по созданию «Долины ЦОДов» — Казахтелеком обеспечивает инфраструктуру, превращая энергию Экибастуза в экспортный цифровой продукт.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Подписан пакет соглашений между Казахстаном, Firebird и NVIDIA на сумму $10 млрд в присутствии Премьер-министра Олжаса Бектенова\n• Bloomberg выделил Казахстан как новую точку роста глобальной AI-индустрии\n• Первый этап: $5 млрд инвестиций, из которых $1 млрд — от Казахтелекома; запуск первой очереди 125 МВт запланирован на 2027 год\n• Второй этап: ещё $5 млрд, параметры будут определены дополнительно\n• Firebird привносит международную экспертизу и клиентов, NVIDIA — технологии, Казахстан — площадку, энергию и инфраструктуру\n• Казахтелеком отвечает за связь, энергетическую инфраструктуру, инженерные решения, надёжность и масштабирование\n• 2026 год объявлен Годом цифровизации и искусственного интеллекта в Казахстане\n• Стратегия: экспортировать не электроэнергию, а вычислительные мощности и цифровые сервисы\n\n💾 <i>Крупнейшая AI-инфраструктурная сделка в Центральной Азии, зафиксированная Bloomberg — показательный кейс того, как энергетические преимущества региона конвертируются в цифровой экспорт.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DZmhWrXiBxU/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#казахстан #ai-инфраструктура #nvidia</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Казахстан: $10 млрд AI-сделка с NVIDIA</b><br><i>Казахстан, Firebird и NVIDIA подписали пакет соглашений на $10 млрд по созданию «Долины ЦОДов» — Казахтелеком обеспечивает инфраструктуру, превращая энергию Экибастуза в экспортный цифровой продукт.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Подписан пакет соглашений между Казахстаном, Firebird и NVIDIA на сумму $10 млрд в присутствии Премьер-министра Олжаса Бектенова</li><li>Bloomberg выделил Казахстан как новую точку роста глобальной AI-индустрии</li><li>Первый этап: $5 млрд инвестиций, из которых $1 млрд — от Казахтелекома; запуск первой очереди 125 МВт запланирован на 2027 год</li><li>Второй этап: ещё $5 млрд, параметры будут определены дополнительно</li><li>Firebird привносит международную экспертизу и клиентов, NVIDIA — технологии, Казахстан — площадку, энергию и инфраструктуру</li><li>Казахтелеком отвечает за связь, энергетическую инфраструктуру, инженерные решения, надёжность и масштабирование</li><li>2026 год объявлен Годом цифровизации и искусственного интеллекта в Казахстане</li><li>Стратегия: экспортировать не электроэнергию, а вычислительные мощности и цифровые сервисы</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Крупнейшая AI-инфраструктурная сделка в Центральной Азии, зафиксированная Bloomberg — показательный кейс того, как энергетические преимущества региона конвертируются в цифровой экспорт.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DZmhWrXiBxU/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#казахстан #ai-инфраструктура #nvidia</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Казахстан, Firebird и NVIDIA подписали соглашения на $10 млрд по строительству «Долины ЦОДов». Первый этап — $5 млрд, запуск 125 МВт в 2027 году. Казахтелеком обеспечивает инфраструктуру. Цель — превратить энергетику Экибастуза в экспорт вычислительных мощностей. Bloomberg признал Казахстан новым AI-хабом.\n\n<b>Slide 1</b> — <i>Групповое фото делегаций на фоне герба Казахстана и государственного флага — официальная церемония подписания соглашений</i>\n\n<b>Slide 2</b> — <i>Скриншот статьи Bloomberg о сделке Казахстана, Firebird и Nvidia на $10 млрд</i>\nBloomberg\nTechnology | AI\nKazakhstan, Firebird Ink $10 Billion AI Deal With Nvidia Support\nBy Nariman Gizitdinov and Greg Sullivan\nJune 15, 2026 at 12:00 PM GMT+5\nKazakhstan signed accords with the startup Firebird Inc. on computing projects involving Nvidia Corp. that could bring as much as $10 billion in investment, as the Central Asian energy producer looks to position itself as an artificial intelligence hub.\n\n<b>Slide 3</b> — <i>Переговоры за круглым столом: представитель Firebird (мужчина в тёмно-синем пиджаке) выступает перед казахстанской стороной</i>\n\n<b>Slide 4</b> — <i>Казахстанская сторона за переговорным столом — предположительно Премьер-министр Олжас Бектенов в центре</i>\n\n<b>Slide 5</b> — <i>Церемония подписания соглашений: двое подписывают документы за столом с цветами, Премьер-министр стоит в центре на фоне герба и флага Казахстана</i>\n\n<b>Slide 6</b> — <i>Портрет мужчины в синем пиджаке с красным галстуком — предположительно Багдат Мусин (глава Казахтелекома) во время переговоров</i></details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-15T14:43:32"
  },
