    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Best Independent Journalists to Follow</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.dropsitenews.com/\">DropSite News</a> — Ryan Grim, Jeremy Scahill\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.kenklippenstein.com/\">Ken Klippenstein</a> — Ken Klippenstein\n✅ <a href=\"https://courtneybonneau.com/\">Courtney Bonneau</a> — Courtney Bonneau\n⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=Afif+Nasuli+journalist+Gaza+Interval+News\">Afif Nasuli</a> — Afif Nasuli — <i>No independent web presence found; mentioned as journalist who documented Gaza and joined Interval News</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.interval.news/\">Interval News</a> — Hemu Rahman\n\n💾 <i>A vetted shortlist of independent investigative journalists covering stories that major outlets suppress, with direct links to their work.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DY5t08cxYyX/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#journalism #investigative #independent-media</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Best Independent Journalists to Follow</b><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.dropsitenews.com/\">DropSite News</a> — Ryan Grim, Jeremy Scahill</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.kenklippenstein.com/\">Ken Klippenstein</a> — Ken Klippenstein</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://courtneybonneau.com/\">Courtney Bonneau</a> — Courtney Bonneau</li><li>⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=Afif+Nasuli+journalist+Gaza+Interval+News\">Afif Nasuli</a> — Afif Nasuli — <i>No independent web presence found; mentioned as journalist who documented Gaza and joined Interval News</i></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.interval.news/\">Interval News</a> — Hemu Rahman</li></ol><br>💾 <i>A vetted shortlist of independent investigative journalists covering stories that major outlets suppress, with direct links to their work.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DY5t08cxYyX/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#journalism #investigative #independent-media</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Curated recommendations for Ryan Grim and Jeremy Scahill (DropSite News), Ken Klippenstein (national security investigations), Courtney Bonneau (on-the-ground in Lebanon), and Afif Nasuli (documented Gaza firsthand). The author also promotes Interval News, his own platform built to aggregate this kind of independent reporting.\n\nIt&#x27;s surprisingly hard to figure out what&#x27;s actually happening in the world, so I want to shout out my favorite independent journalists who have not been bought out. The ones who are risking a lot for you and I, as they investigate our puppet masters and cover the things that we&#x27;re generally not supposed to know about. Now, all of these are my favorites, but I&#x27;m saving one of the best for last. First, we have Ryan Grimm and Jeremy Scahill, the founders of DropSite News. DropSite is arguably the most important outlet you need to be following daily. They&#x27;re actually a big inspiration for why I started Interval. They broke the first story of the white and blue flag state sending spies to stay with Jeffrey Epstein for weeks at a time, and when they published that article, no major outlet wanted to touch it. So I thought, why not build a news platform that isn&#x27;t afraid, to make that the highlighted story of the day? Next, we have Ken Klippenstein, and Ken is not afraid to hold back. He&#x27;s single-handedly done most of the investigations around the new definition of domestic terrorism in the U.S. He didn&#x27;t hesitate to cover how the U.S. spies on the Vatican, and even ICE&#x27;s secret watch list of Americans. The things that you and I need to be very aware of. Third, we have Courtney, who is literally on the ground in Lebanon. In case you missed it, the white and blue state said they&#x27;re using the Gaza playbook on Lebanon, and they&#x27;re flattening entire neighborhoods. Courtney has been on the ground, capturing first-hand footage to make sure that the winners aren&#x27;t the ones who are going to write history. And last but not least, we&#x27;ve got Afif Nasuli. This one&#x27;s special because we just hired Afif to join our team, which is arguably the biggest milestone for Interval. He was the only journalist that managed to sneak into Gaza, where he spent months volunteering while also documenting the horrors. If you subscribe to Interval News, you are officially paying for his rent and empowering him to continue all the investigations that really matter. I&#x27;m the founder of Interval News, and we&#x27;re going to make a dent in the world. We&#x27;re going to be the one platform that does not shy away from the stories that matter most. The ones we know are often getting suppressed or outright censored. Sure, we&#x27;ll highlight the big headlines when Trump is threatening to erase another civilization, but our main mission is to highlight the independent journalists that matter way more. If you&#x27;re an investigative journalist, please reach out, because it&#x27;s your shoulders that we all stand on. It&#x27;s more important now than ever before that we all stay informed so we&#x27;re not being manipulated. I&#x27;ll catch you in the next one.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-15T20:56:55"
  },
