    "markdown": "“<b>Verily Allah does not change the condition of people until they change what is in themselves</b>”<br>— Author not clear<br><i>Islamic practices like zikr, salah, and gratitude are neurological rewiring sessions that operate through the same mechanisms neuroscience now describes as RAS filtering and neuroplasticity.</i><br>💡 <b>Your dominant thoughts determine what your brain perceives as possible, and Islamic acts of worship are — neurologically — repeated belief-reinforcement sessions.</b><br>💾 <i>Frames Islamic devotional practices through a neuroscience lens, offering a dual spiritual and scientific rationale for zikr, gratitude, and positive belief.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZDvudMtdrn/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#neuroscience #islam #mindset</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>The creator connects the neuroscience of the RAS and neuroplasticity to Quranic verse 13:11 and the Hadith Qudsi about thinking well of Allah. The argument: Islamic practices (zikr, salah, shukr) are, in neurological terms, repeated sessions of belief reinforcement that reshape dominant thought patterns, cortisol/dopamine balance, and ultimately what opportunities the brain perceives — matching what neuroscience now calls RAS filtering and neuroplasticity.\n\nscientists just discovered that your brain is literally programmed to make you rich and islam knew about this 1400 years ago what the brain researchers found was your ras system which is a filter in your brain decides what reality you see so when you tell your brain what you want with emotion repetition and belief the ras starts finding opportunities people and solutions that were always there but were invisible to you and no this isn&#x27;t some sort of a fantasy this is neuroscience neuroplasticity your brain literally rewires self around your dominant thoughts other than that students from harvard stanford and a neuroscientist show that people who visualize their goals with gratitude and belief physically changes their brain structure within weeks their cortisol drops their dopamine spikes and so they take better decisions and they attract better opportunities as well so in return their income relationships and health all shift the amazing yet shocking fact about your brain that it cannot tell the difference between vividly imagined reality and a real one now here is when it really gets powerful allah says in the quran verily allah does not change the condition of people until they change what what is in themselves that&#x27;s the ras that&#x27;s neuroplasticity 1400 years before neuroscience had a name for it and the prophet peace be upon him also said that allah says i am as my servant thinks of me as so by that law if you think allah is gonna provide your brain opens to see the provision on the contrary if you think you&#x27;re always gonna struggle your ras filters out every opportunity so zikr salah gratitude shukar all of these aren&#x27;t just acts of worship these are neurological rewiring sessions every single time you do them</details>",
