  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXNWiUujTZl/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Face It Framework for Avoidance</b>\n<i>“Clarity doesn&#x27;t come from thinking more. It comes from facing things.”</i>\n\n🪜 <b>How to</b>\n1. Write down the one specific thing you&#x27;ve been avoiding — not a list, just one thing\n2. Write what you think will happen if you do it — don&#x27;t filter, be honest about what you&#x27;re afraid of\n3. Write what exactly happens if you never do it\n4. Write how you would handle it if the worst case actually happened\n\n<i>Useful for: Anyone who knows what they are procrastinating on but doesn&#x27;t know how to face it.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Provides a concrete 4-step written exercise that converts vague avoidance into a clear, actionable path forward in five minutes.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXNWiUujTZl/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#procrastination #avoidance #clarity</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Face It Framework for Avoidance</b><br><i>“Clarity doesn&#x27;t come from thinking more. It comes from facing things.”</i><br>🪜 <b>How to</b><br><ol><li>Write down the one specific thing you&#x27;ve been avoiding — not a list, just one thing</li><li>Write what you think will happen if you do it — don&#x27;t filter, be honest about what you&#x27;re afraid of</li><li>Write what exactly happens if you never do it</li><li>Write how you would handle it if the worst case actually happened</li></ol><br><i>Useful for: Anyone who knows what they are procrastinating on but doesn&#x27;t know how to face it.</i><br>💾 <i>Provides a concrete 4-step written exercise that converts vague avoidance into a clear, actionable path forward in five minutes.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXNWiUujTZl/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#procrastination #avoidance #clarity</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>The creator presents the Face It Framework: write down the one thing you&#x27;re avoiding, what you fear will happen if you act, what happens if you never act, and how you&#x27;d handle the worst case. The core argument is that what feels like confusion is actually avoidance, and writing it out reveals you already know what to do.\n\nThis is the exercise that forces you to stop avoiding your life. Most people know exactly what they&#x27;re procrastinating on, but they don&#x27;t know how to face it. This is called the face it framework. It takes five minutes and it will show you exactly how to move forward. First, write down what you&#x27;ve been avoiding. Be specific. Not a list, just one thing. Second, write what you think will happen if you do it. Don&#x27;t filter it, just be honest about what you&#x27;ve been afraid of. Third, write what exactly happens if you never do it. This is the part most people don&#x27;t think about. And last, write how you would handle it if the worst case actually happened. When you see it written out, you&#x27;ll realize it&#x27;s not fear, it&#x27;s avoidance. Clarity doesn&#x27;t come from thinking more. It comes from facing things. You&#x27;re not confused. You already know what to do. You&#x27;re just avoiding it.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-29T00:06:00"
  },
