  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ6dYQONPGY/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>10 Must-Watch YouTube Videos</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zjkBMFhNj_g\">Deep Dive into LLMs like ChatGPT</a> — Andrej Karpathy — <i>Search confirms Karpathy has a video titled &#x27;Deep dive into LLMs like ChatGPT&#x27;; link provided is his &#x27;[1hr Talk] Intro to Large Language Models&#x27; — the specific deep dive video URL could not be confirmed from search results directly.</i>\n⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RK_9bqOac9U\">The Formula that Broke Wall Street</a> — Author not clear — <i>Closest title match from search for the transcript&#x27;s &#x27;equation that broke Wall Street&#x27;; however the transcript describes a physics equation that built the derivatives industry (Black-Scholes), while this video covers the Gaussian Copula — exact video the Reel recommends is uncertain.</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UF8uR6Z6KLc\">Steve Jobs&#x27; 2005 Stanford Commencement Address</a> — Stanford University\n⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F4txhN13y6A\">Psychology: The Stanford Prison Experiment</a> — BBC — <i>Multiple Stanford Prison Experiment videos on YouTube; BBC Documentary is the most credible result but the specific video the Reel recommends is not confirmed.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Curated shortlist of highly-rated YouTube videos spanning AI fundamentals, finance history, leadership, and psychology — each covering a foundational idea from a different domain.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ6dYQONPGY/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#youtube #recommendations #learning</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>10 Must-Watch YouTube Videos</b><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zjkBMFhNj_g\">Deep Dive into LLMs like ChatGPT</a> — Andrej Karpathy — <i>Search confirms Karpathy has a video titled &#x27;Deep dive into LLMs like ChatGPT&#x27;; link provided is his &#x27;[1hr Talk] Intro to Large Language Models&#x27; — the specific deep dive video URL could not be confirmed from search results directly.</i></li><li>⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RK_9bqOac9U\">The Formula that Broke Wall Street</a> — Author not clear — <i>Closest title match from search for the transcript&#x27;s &#x27;equation that broke Wall Street&#x27;; however the transcript describes a physics equation that built the derivatives industry (Black-Scholes), while this video covers the Gaussian Copula — exact video the Reel recommends is uncertain.</i></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UF8uR6Z6KLc\">Steve Jobs&#x27; 2005 Stanford Commencement Address</a> — Stanford University</li><li>⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=F4txhN13y6A\">Psychology: The Stanford Prison Experiment</a> — BBC — <i>Multiple Stanford Prison Experiment videos on YouTube; BBC Documentary is the most credible result but the specific video the Reel recommends is not confirmed.</i></li></ol><br>💾 <i>Curated shortlist of highly-rated YouTube videos spanning AI fundamentals, finance history, leadership, and psychology — each covering a foundational idea from a different domain.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ6dYQONPGY/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#youtube #recommendations #learning</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Reel recommends four YouTube videos: Andrej Karpathy&#x27;s LLM deep dive to understand how ChatGPT and Claude work, a video on the physics equation that built the derivatives industry, Steve Jobs&#x27; 2005 Stanford commencement address on dropping out, getting fired, and cancer, and a documentary on the Stanford Prison Experiment and unchecked power.\n\n10 out of 10 YouTube videos to be the most interesting person at the table. Deep dive into LLMs by Andreech Karpathy to understand how models like Chachaviti and Claude actually work. The equation that broke Wall Street. Watch how a physics equation built the entire finance industry on derivatives. Steve Jobs&#x27; 2005 commencing speech where he talks about dropping out, getting fired from Apple, and getting a cancer diagnosis. The Stanford Prison Experiment exposes a dark side of human nature that comes with unchecked power.</details>",
