  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ_3qpXvfn6/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>you either win or you quit. If you try enough times, it eventually will happen.</b>”\n— Author not clear\n\n<i>In a system where every state has a non-zero transition probability, the system is ergodic, meaning sufficient repetitions make eventual success mathematically guaranteed.</i>\n💡 <b>Quitting is the only real failure — persistence is mathematically guaranteed to work in an ergodic system.</b>\n\n💾 <i>Uses ergodic theory to give the persistence principle mathematical rigor rather than just motivational appeal.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ_3qpXvfn6/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#persistence #ergodicity #mindset</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>you either win or you quit. If you try enough times, it eventually will happen.</b>”<br>— Author not clear<br><i>In a system where every state has a non-zero transition probability, the system is ergodic, meaning sufficient repetitions make eventual success mathematically guaranteed.</i><br>💡 <b>Quitting is the only real failure — persistence is mathematically guaranteed to work in an ergodic system.</b><br>💾 <i>Uses ergodic theory to give the persistence principle mathematical rigor rather than just motivational appeal.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ_3qpXvfn6/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#persistence #ergodicity #mindset</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>If a system is ergodic — every state reachable with non-zero probability — enough repetitions drive false-negative probability to zero. Applied to life: the only way to not succeed is to stop trying.\n\nMathematically, in a system where each state has a non-zero transition probability, the system is actually ergodic. So if you have enough repetitions for a cause, you will eventually drive the false negatives probability to zero. But simply I could have said that you either win or you quit. If you try enough times, it eventually will happen.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-28T23:58:02"
  },
  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaD7eNlTnj3/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>10 YouTube Videos Learn AI Agents</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EH5jx5qPabU\">From Zero to Your First AI Agent in 25 Minutes (No Coding)</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Lg-meK5IU8Q\">What AI Agent Skills Are and How They Work</a> — IBM Technology\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@IBMTechnology/videos\">IBM Technology</a> — IBM\n⚠️ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FwOTs4UxQS4\">AI Agents, Clearly Explained</a> — Jeff Su — <i>Title matches transcript phrasing but authorship as Jeff Su not confirmed from search results alone; could not verify the Google Meet/Notion/Slack integration content</i>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Retrieval-augmented_generation\">RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)</a>\n⚠️ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Model_Context_Protocol\">MCP (Model Context Protocol)</a> — <i>Mentioned as a concept the IBM Technology video explains clearly; Wikipedia article existence not confirmed</i>\n\n💾 <i>Vetted shortlist of beginner-to-intermediate YouTube videos on AI agents saves time hunting for quality starting points.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaD7eNlTnj3/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#ai-agents #youtube #learning</i>",
