    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>4 YouTube Channels to Learn LLMs</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCYO_jab_esuFRV4b17AJtAw\">3Blue1Brown</a> — Grant Sanderson\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLoROMvodv4rOaMFbaqxPDoLWjDaRAdP9D\">Stanford CS224N: NLP with Deep Learning (Spring 2024)</a> — Christopher Manning\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@AndrejKarpathy\">Andrej Karpathy</a> — Andrej Karpathy\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKWaEZ-_VweaEx1j62do_vQ\">IBM Technology</a> — IBM\n\n💾 <i>Curated map of four free YouTube resources for learning LLMs, each matched to a distinct learning style.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZtMidqNeyU/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#llm #learning #youtube</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>4 YouTube Channels to Learn LLMs</b><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCYO_jab_esuFRV4b17AJtAw\">3Blue1Brown</a> — Grant Sanderson</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLoROMvodv4rOaMFbaqxPDoLWjDaRAdP9D\">Stanford CS224N: NLP with Deep Learning (Spring 2024)</a> — Christopher Manning</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@AndrejKarpathy\">Andrej Karpathy</a> — Andrej Karpathy</li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCKWaEZ-_VweaEx1j62do_vQ\">IBM Technology</a> — IBM</li></ol><br>💾 <i>Curated map of four free YouTube resources for learning LLMs, each matched to a distinct learning style.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZtMidqNeyU/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#llm #learning #youtube</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Four YouTube channels for building a concrete understanding of LLMs — 3Blue1Brown for visual explanations, Stanford CS224N for lecture-style depth, Andrej Karpathy for watching an LLM built from scratch in real time, and IBM Technology for conceptual coverage without heavy technical detail.\n\nFour YouTube videos that will give you an extremely concrete basis on LLMs. If you want a visual explanation, I would go with 3 brown, 1 blue. For a more lecture-style explanation, I would go with Stanford Engineering CS classes. To see how an LLM is built out in real time, Karpathy&#x27;s channel is an absolute goldmine. If you want to learn all the concepts behind LLMs but don&#x27;t want to go too technical, then IBM&#x27;s explanation is perfect for you.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-06-28T23:56:35"
