  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ8Hr1BvZpx/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>10 Concepts That Explain Luck</b>\n<i>“if you knew all of these then you understand how the world works better than 99 of people”</i>\n\n📚 <b>Concepts</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_law\">Power law</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base_rate_fallacy\">Base rate fallacy</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expected_value\">Expected value</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Survivorship_bias\">Survivorship bias</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawthorne_effect\">Hawthorne effect</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simpson%27s_paradox\">Simpson&#x27;s paradox</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regression_toward_the_mean\">Regression to the mean</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Petersburg_paradox\">St. Petersburg paradox</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abraham_Wald\">Abraham Wald problem</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkson%27s_paradox\">Berkson&#x27;s paradox</a>\n\n💾 <i>Compact checklist of 10 named statistical and probability concepts that explain how luck, bias, and chance actually operate.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ8Hr1BvZpx/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#probability #statistics #cognitive-bias</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>10 Concepts That Explain Luck</b><br><i>“if you knew all of these then you understand how the world works better than 99 of people”</i><br>📚 <b>Concepts</b><br><ol><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_law\">Power law</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base_rate_fallacy\">Base rate fallacy</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expected_value\">Expected value</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Survivorship_bias\">Survivorship bias</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawthorne_effect\">Hawthorne effect</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simpson%27s_paradox\">Simpson&#x27;s paradox</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regression_toward_the_mean\">Regression to the mean</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St._Petersburg_paradox\">St. Petersburg paradox</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abraham_Wald\">Abraham Wald problem</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berkson%27s_paradox\">Berkson&#x27;s paradox</a></li></ol><br>💾 <i>Compact checklist of 10 named statistical and probability concepts that explain how luck, bias, and chance actually operate.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZ8Hr1BvZpx/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#probability #statistics #cognitive-bias</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>jadeneoca lists 10 named concepts in probability and statistics (power law, base rate fallacy, expected value, survivorship bias, Hawthorne effect, Simpson&#x27;s paradox, regression to the mean, St. Petersburg paradox, Abraham Wald problem, Berkson&#x27;s paradox) and claims knowing all of them puts you ahead of 99% of people in understanding how the world works.\n\nlet&#x27;s see if you actually understand luck but it&#x27;s extremely neat power law base theorem expected value survivorship bias hawthorne effect simpson&#x27;s paradox regression to the mean st petersburg paradox the abraham wald problem lastly berkson&#x27;s paradox if you knew all of these then you understand how the world works better than 99 of people</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
