    "digest": "“<b>We cheer for persistence differently than we cheer for talent, because persistence looks like a choice, which means it was possible and we could have made it too, and maybe we still can.</b>”\n— curiousnoor\n\n<i>Vozinha&#x27;s 19-year journey — driving buses, playing across seven divisions — to Cape Verde&#x27;s historic 0-0 draw against Spain at age 40 is proof that &#x27;not yet&#x27; and &#x27;never&#x27; are not the same thing.</i>\n💡 <b>Not yet and never are not the same thing — and most of us make that mistake about ourselves before anyone else gets the chance.</b>\n\n💾 <i>A precise, sourced story that makes the &#x27;your timeline is not behind&#x27; principle concrete through a vivid real-world example.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSCqS51Tb/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#persistence #timeline #football</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>We cheer for persistence differently than we cheer for talent, because persistence looks like a choice, which means it was possible and we could have made it too, and maybe we still can.</b>”<br>— curiousnoor<br><i>Vozinha&#x27;s 19-year journey — driving buses, playing across seven divisions — to Cape Verde&#x27;s historic 0-0 draw against Spain at age 40 is proof that &#x27;not yet&#x27; and &#x27;never&#x27; are not the same thing.</i><br>💡 <b>Not yet and never are not the same thing — and most of us make that mistake about ourselves before anyone else gets the chance.</b><br>💾 <i>A precise, sourced story that makes the &#x27;your timeline is not behind&#x27; principle concrete through a vivid real-world example.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://vt.tiktok.com/ZSCqS51Tb/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#persistence #timeline #football</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Vozinha turned pro at 25 after scouts passed him twice, worked odd jobs to stay in football, played across six countries and seven divisions over 19 years, then kept a clean sheet against Spain at the 2026 World Cup at age 40. The reel uses his story to illustrate that your timeline is not behind — it&#x27;s just yours.</details>",
