    "digest": "<b>Three Essential NYC Resource Websites</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://5pm.nyc/\">5pm.nyc</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.nyctrivialist.com/\">NYC Trivia List</a>\n⚠️ <a href=\"https://linedance.nyc\">linedance.nyc</a> — <i>Search returned only the Instagram account @linedance.nyc; standalone website https://linedance.nyc not confirmed in search results. Described in the reel as a Google Sheets-based resource with event listings, 480-song tutorial database, and local cobbler directory.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Curates three hard-to-discover NYC-specific directories that replace tedious Google Maps searching for happy hours, trivia nights, and line dancing.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaVzj93MO9j/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#nyc #nightlife #resources</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Three Essential NYC Resource Websites</b><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>✅ <a href=\"https://5pm.nyc/\">5pm.nyc</a></li><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.nyctrivialist.com/\">NYC Trivia List</a></li><li>⚠️ <a href=\"https://linedance.nyc\">linedance.nyc</a> — <i>Search returned only the Instagram account @linedance.nyc; standalone website https://linedance.nyc not confirmed in search results. Described in the reel as a Google Sheets-based resource with event listings, 480-song tutorial database, and local cobbler directory.</i></li></ol><br>💾 <i>Curates three hard-to-discover NYC-specific directories that replace tedious Google Maps searching for happy hours, trivia nights, and line dancing.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaVzj93MO9j/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#nyc #nightlife #resources</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>A roundup of three unofficial but highly useful NYC city guides — a happy hour finder searchable by zip code and neighborhood, a trivia night directory filterable by day and borough, and a line dancing resource with event schedules, a 480-song linked tutorial database, and a cobbler listing.\n\nthree websites every city should have. Number one, 5pm.nyc. This is a website guide for all of the happy hours happening across all the boroughs. You can look by zip code, by neighborhood, by address. When you do your little search, there&#x27;s all the information you always wanted. Seating type, food, cost, there&#x27;s drink type. Really eliminates the struggle of going through Google Maps. And then even like calling the places. Do you have a happy hour? Who knows, you know, but now we do. Number two, NYC trivia lists. This is a website where there&#x27;s an entire list of all the trivia going on across all five boroughs. You can search by borough or by day of the week and you can see where trivia is going on. So you can always go to trivia. Kind of goes hand in hand with the happy hour a little bit. Number three, linedance.nyc. This is an informal website, basically a Google Sheets with all the information you could want on line dancing. They have local line dancing, when they are, how much they are. Then they have a huge database of 480 songs with linked tutorials, how to teach yourself. They have a page for cobblers. So if you need to get your cowboy shoes fixed, local cobblers. I rest my case.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-07-04T02:18:01"
