    "digest": "“<b>Are you climbing a mountain for the world to see you or for you to see the world?</b>”\n— lulu.broski\n\n<i>A single rhetorical question challenging whether your ambitions are driven by the desire for external recognition or genuine personal experience.</i>\n💡 <b>Do things for the view, not to be seen.</b>\n\n💾 <i>A concise, memorable question that cuts to the core of intrinsic vs. extrinsic motivation.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaSx0F0AFLz/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#motivation #ego #introspection</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>Are you climbing a mountain for the world to see you or for you to see the world?</b>”<br>— lulu.broski<br><i>A single rhetorical question challenging whether your ambitions are driven by the desire for external recognition or genuine personal experience.</i><br>💡 <b>Do things for the view, not to be seen.</b><br>💾 <i>A concise, memorable question that cuts to the core of intrinsic vs. extrinsic motivation.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaSx0F0AFLz/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#motivation #ego #introspection</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>One question: are you climbing to be seen, or to see? A sharp prompt for examining the real motivation behind your goals.\n\nAre you climbing a mountain for the world to see you or for you to see the world?</details>",
