    "digest": "<b>AI-Printed Daily Morning Newspaper</b>\n<i>Use Claude or Codex to auto-generate a personalized daily briefing that prints each morning with weather, texts, emails, and urgent alerts — so you get your update without touching your phone.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Research shows checking your phone first thing in the morning (and before bed) is harmful\n• The printed briefing covers weather, texts, emails, and flags anything urgent enough to warrant opening your phone\n• Physical paper removes the compulsive scroll — you get the signal without the noise\n\n💾 <i>Practical AI automation pattern that solves the phone-first-thing habit with a physical printed briefing.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DadgRrstvSw/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#productivity #morning-routine #ai</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>AI-Printed Daily Morning Newspaper</b><br><i>Use Claude or Codex to auto-generate a personalized daily briefing that prints each morning with weather, texts, emails, and urgent alerts — so you get your update without touching your phone.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Research shows checking your phone first thing in the morning (and before bed) is harmful</li><li>The printed briefing covers weather, texts, emails, and flags anything urgent enough to warrant opening your phone</li><li>Physical paper removes the compulsive scroll — you get the signal without the noise</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Practical AI automation pattern that solves the phone-first-thing habit with a physical printed briefing.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DadgRrstvSw/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#productivity #morning-routine #ai</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>An AI agent (Claude or Codex) compiles your weather, texts, and emails into a daily printed briefing delivered to your home printer every morning. The goal is breaking the habit of checking your phone first thing — you get all the signal on paper without opening any app. The creator offers a ready-made skill for replicating the setup.\n\nThis guy figured out something really cool. You can actually get Codex or Claude to create a daily newspaper just for him. And we all know we shouldn&#x27;t be going on our phones first thing in the morning, and yet we still do. There&#x27;s always a justification. Maybe there&#x27;s a text. Maybe there&#x27;s something urgent that I need to reply to, an email, a Slack message. This guy figured out something really cool. You can actually get Codex or Claude to create a daily newspaper just for him. Prints from his printer every morning, and every morning it gives him an update on the weather, on text, on his emails, and if there&#x27;s anything urgent that he should check on his phone. So it&#x27;s a nice way to get updated on the things that matter to you without having to touch your phone screen, because the studies are all out there. Phone first thing in the morning and first thing before bed is bad for you. If you want to do this yourself, I made a skill. Comment newspaper, and I&#x27;ll send it to you, and you&#x27;ll be able to set it up with your own printer at home with Claude or Codex.</details>",
