<i>Three-panel slide: top shows leafy greens (gut-brain axis), middle shows a medical chalkboard with brain anatomy diagrams (neuroplasticity), bottom shows a reddish-brown close-up (microbiome)</i>\nThe Gut-Brain Axis\nNeuroplasticity\nMicrobiome\n\n<b>Slide 3</b> — <i>Three-panel slide: top shows a wall covered in handwritten notes (cognitive biases), middle shows a DNA double-helix sculpture in a museum (epigenetics), bottom shows white curtains with warm lamp light (hormonal feedback loops)</i>\nCognitive biases\nEpigenetics\nHormonal feedback loops\n\n<b>Slide 4</b> — <i>Three-panel slide: top shows a bed being made (sleep architecture), middle shows people crossing a street from above (decision fatigue), bottom shows iced drinks and paper bags on a table (placebo effect)</i>\nSleep architecture\nDecision fatigue\nThe placebo effect</details>",
