  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dak5tJ5ICTl/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>I happen to believe that the art of life is holding both without letting either win.</b>”\n— diewithoutregretss\n\n<i>12-year-old you would be proud of where you are, and 80-year-old you would push you further — the tension between those two isn&#x27;t a flaw, it&#x27;s what gives life meaning.</i>\n💡 <b>A heart that says &#x27;I&#x27;m already enough&#x27; and a head that says &#x27;be more anyway&#x27; can coexist — that tension is the point, not a problem.</b>\n\n💾 <i>Concise articulation of how gratitude and ambition aren&#x27;t opposites but two forces that together create a meaningful life.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dak5tJ5ICTl/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#mindset #ambition #gratitude</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>I happen to believe that the art of life is holding both without letting either win.</b>”<br>— diewithoutregretss<br><i>12-year-old you would be proud of where you are, and 80-year-old you would push you further — the tension between those two isn&#x27;t a flaw, it&#x27;s what gives life meaning.</i><br>💡 <b>A heart that says &#x27;I&#x27;m already enough&#x27; and a head that says &#x27;be more anyway&#x27; can coexist — that tension is the point, not a problem.</b><br>💾 <i>Concise articulation of how gratitude and ambition aren&#x27;t opposites but two forces that together create a meaningful life.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dak5tJ5ICTl/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#mindset #ambition #gratitude</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>A short philosophical take on holding gratitude and hunger at the same time. Uses the frame of a 12-year-old self vs. an 80-year-old self to show that both perspectives are valid and necessary. The tension between them isn&#x27;t something to resolve — it&#x27;s what makes life meaningful.\n\nThe paradox of being a high achiever is that 12-year-old you would be so damn proud if they could see you right now. And 80-year-old you would probably laugh at how small you&#x27;re still playing. I love this frame because it&#x27;s a beautiful reminder that you can simultaneously hold deep gratitude for where you&#x27;re at and relentless hunger for where you&#x27;re going. A heart that says, I know I&#x27;m already enough. A head that says, be more anyway. I happen to believe that the art of life is holding both without letting either win. And that tension between the two isn&#x27;t a problem. That&#x27;s what gives life meaning. It&#x27;s the whole fucking point.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-07-09T23:37:54"
  },
  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DambEp1igDW/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Perfect Short-Form Script Structure</b>\n<i>A 7-part scripting template — Hook, Lead, Body, Open Loop (×2), and CTA — maximizes retention and converts the most engaged viewers.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Hook breaks the pattern of what viewers see in the feed\n• Lead pulls viewers to the 10-second bar so they stop scrolling\n• Body 1 introduces the first piece of value\n• Open Loop 1 creates curiosity to keep watching (e.g. &#x27;yet that&#x27;s not the craziest part&#x27;)\n• Body 2 delivers a second piece of value\n• Open Loop 2 adds another curiosity spike (e.g. a surprising fact or unexpected twist)\n• Body 3 delivers the final piece of value\n• CTA takes the warmest viewers to the next step (e.g. &#x27;comment [keyword] to get value&#x27;)\n• Repeat the Body + Open Loop structure twice before the CTA\n\n💾 <i>Gives a concrete, repeatable 7-part script template that addresses both retention and conversion for short-form video.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DambEp1igDW/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#scripting #short-form #retention</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Perfect Short-Form Script Structure</b><br><i>A 7-part scripting template — Hook, Lead, Body, Open Loop (×2), and CTA — maximizes retention and converts the most engaged viewers.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Hook breaks the pattern of what viewers see in the feed</li><li>Lead pulls viewers to the 10-second bar so they stop scrolling</li><li>Body 1 introduces the first piece of value</li><li>Open Loop 1 creates curiosity to keep watching (e.g. &#x27;yet that&#x27;s not the craziest part&#x27;)</li><li>Body 2 delivers a second piece of value</li><li>Open Loop 2 adds another curiosity spike (e.g. a surprising fact or unexpected twist)</li><li>Body 3 delivers the final piece of value</li><li>CTA takes the warmest viewers to the next step (e.g. &#x27;comment [keyword] to get value&#x27;)</li><li>Repeat the Body + Open Loop structure twice before the CTA</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Gives a concrete, repeatable 7-part script template that addresses both retention and conversion for short-form video.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DambEp1igDW/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#scripting #short-form #retention</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>The reel teaches a repeatable short-form scripting formula. The hook disrupts the scroll; the lead anchors viewers past the 10-second mark; two rounds of Body + Open Loop stack value and curiosity; the CTA converts the most engaged viewers into the next step of the funnel.\n\nhook lead body one open loop one body two open loop two body three cta this is the perfect structure for short form content in the hook and the lead the hook breaks the pattern of what they see the lead pulls them to the 10 second bar once they&#x27;re anchored there they&#x27;re not scrolling off body one introduced the first piece of value open loops create more curiosity yet that&#x27;s not the craziest part and funnily enough in 1893 richard fyman but we couldn&#x27;t have expected to get this bad you&#x27;re gonna repeat that structure two times and lastly the cta takes your warmest viewers and puts them into the next step of the fun comment keywords to get value dot dot and that is the perfect structure of short form content</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-07-10T09:27:25"
  },
