  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXcCtVIiO28/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Inversion Mental Model Explained</b>\n<i>Inversion is a mental model where you outline the opposite of what you want to happen — asking what guarantees failure — to build better plans and challenge hidden assumptions.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Avoiding failure and achieving success are two separate questions that deserve equal weight.\n• Ask &#x27;If I were terrible at X, what would I do every day?&#x27; — then avoid exactly those things.\n• Seek the answer not only from yourself but from people with more or different experience.\n• Inversion forces you to challenge your beliefs, not just reinforce them.\n\n💾 <i>A concise, example-driven explanation of the inversion mental model and its Stoic roots, useful for anyone building better decision-making habits.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXcCtVIiO28/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#inversion #stoicism #decision-making</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Inversion Mental Model Explained</b><br><i>Inversion is a mental model where you outline the opposite of what you want to happen — asking what guarantees failure — to build better plans and challenge hidden assumptions.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Avoiding failure and achieving success are two separate questions that deserve equal weight.</li><li>Ask &#x27;If I were terrible at X, what would I do every day?&#x27; — then avoid exactly those things.</li><li>Seek the answer not only from yourself but from people with more or different experience.</li><li>Inversion forces you to challenge your beliefs, not just reinforce them.</li></ul><br>💾 <i>A concise, example-driven explanation of the inversion mental model and its Stoic roots, useful for anyone building better decision-making habits.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXcCtVIiO28/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#inversion #stoicism #decision-making</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>The reel introduces inversion: instead of only asking how to succeed, also ask what would guarantee failure, then avoid those things. Rooted in Stoic premeditatio malorum (premeditation of evil), the practice helps overcome fear, expose blind spots, and produce more durable plans. Illustrated with a leadership example and the author&#x27;s husband&#x27;s habit of asking &#x27;How do I fuck this up?&#x27; of people he respects.\n\nWhen you are so focused on trying to achieve success, you forget about the most important part, and that&#x27;s how to avoid failure. These are two separate things, and the greatest thinkers and innovators naturally do this. If you do this, you&#x27;re pretty rare. However, let me explain. This is a mental model called inversion. It&#x27;s basically you outlining the opposite of what you want to happen, and it stems from an exercise that Stoic philosophers would regularly do called prematatio malorum, which translates to premeditation of evil. They believe that if you can envision the worst-case scenario, then you could overcome your fears of the negative consequences and thus create a better plan to prevent them. Now, let&#x27;s put this into a very simple example. I want to be a better leader, so a question I would also consider and answer would be if I were a terrible manager, what would I be doing every single day? And it&#x27;s these things that I would avoid to make sure that my team remains happy and fulfilled. I&#x27;m placing the same amount of weight as me thinking forward and backwards. A better example is the founder of this business podcast, also happens to be my husband. Mark&#x27;s favorite question to ask anyone he admires and respects is, how do I fuck this up, in relation to his business? He&#x27;s not only looking for the answer within himself, he&#x27;s looking for it from other people who have more experience or different experience than him. Inversion forces you to challenge your beliefs, and I&#x27;m all about this. If you like this content, follow along for more. Deeply understanding, though, that these two questions are separate and should be treated as such is why it will be highly effective for you in the long run.</details>",
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-07-21T01:51:41"
  },
