ELENI DI LUZIO\nMAR 12, 2026\n\n<b>Slide 4</b> — <i>Substack article card with a warm-lit photo of two women dining together.</i>\nthe art of asking\non the beauty of deep conversations and a personal archive of questions\nELLA\nAPR 18, 2025\n\n<b>Slide 5</b> — <i>Substack article card featuring a hand-drawn animation still of a stick figure and a boulder.</i>\nHow to become dangerously articulate\n4 ways to start loving uncertainty (and absurdity) in your thinking and in life\nCRAIG PERRY\nDEC 01, 2025\n\n<b>Slide 6</b> — <i>Substack article card with a photo of a classical thinker statue against a blue sky.</i>\nHow to be interesting as F*ck\nWhy most people are forgettable, and what the ones who aren&#x27;t actually do\nSUCCESS NOTES\nMAY 20, 2026\n\n<b>Slide 7</b> — <i>Outro slide — painted scene of a person reading on a train, yellow and white text overlay.</i>\nRead full substacks to build that muscle.\nLink in bio.</details>",
