    "digest": "“<b>You can&#x27;t compete with someone who&#x27;s having fun.</b>”\n— olivianiemann\n\n<i>A content creator arguing that genuine enjoyment of the creative process is an unfair competitive edge that no scarcity-driven competitor can replicate.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Reframes competition as irrelevant when you operate from genuine enjoyment — a durable mindset shift for creators, builders, or anyone in a crowded field.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaoQ4bpBstZ/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#fun #content-creation #mindset</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>You can&#x27;t compete with someone who&#x27;s having fun.</b>”<br>— olivianiemann<br><i>A content creator arguing that genuine enjoyment of the creative process is an unfair competitive edge that no scarcity-driven competitor can replicate.</i><br>💾 <i>Reframes competition as irrelevant when you operate from genuine enjoyment — a durable mindset shift for creators, builders, or anyone in a crowded field.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaoQ4bpBstZ/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#fun #content-creation #mindset</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Short motivational reel built around the hook &#x27;You can&#x27;t compete with someone who&#x27;s having fun.&#x27; The creator argues that doing work as play, embracing beginner energy, and dropping fear-based scarcity makes a person 10x more magnetic — and their own content creation is offered as proof.\n\nYou can&#x27;t compete with someone who&#x27;s having fun. Let fun be your competitive advantage. Let it be the reason that you fall in love with the process of what you&#x27;re doing. If what you&#x27;re doing feels like a chore, you&#x27;re operating from this place of scarcity, of limitation, of fear, rather than just letting yourself play. Let yourself be a beginner. Let the things feel like fun while you&#x27;re doing it because you&#x27;ll be 10 times more magnetic. My competitive advantage is that I have so much fun when I create content. Therefore, you can&#x27;t compete with me. I&#x27;m too busy having fun.</details>",
