  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYDja91vDeD/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Why We Film at Concerts</b>\n<i>“Capturing the moment is part of how we have learned to express excitement and manage emotions that can be overwhelming. The capturing of those feelings has become part of how we experience the feelings themselves.”</i>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/768019/the-story-of-your-life-by-kathryn-jezer-morton/\">The Story of Your Life: How Social Media Shapes the Way We Experience Everything</a> — Kathryn Jezer-Morton\n\n💾 <i>Gives a precise, book-backed explanation for compulsive filming that reframes it as emotional regulation rather than vanity — useful for thinking about presence and attention.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYDja91vDeD/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#social-media #emotion #presence</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Why We Film at Concerts</b><br><i>“Capturing the moment is part of how we have learned to express excitement and manage emotions that can be overwhelming. The capturing of those feelings has become part of how we experience the feelings themselves.”</i><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>✅ <a href=\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/768019/the-story-of-your-life-by-kathryn-jezer-morton/\">The Story of Your Life: How Social Media Shapes the Way We Experience Everything</a> — Kathryn Jezer-Morton</li></ol><br>💾 <i>Gives a precise, book-backed explanation for compulsive filming that reframes it as emotional regulation rather than vanity — useful for thinking about presence and attention.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYDja91vDeD/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#social-media #emotion #presence</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Book excerpt reel explaining why people film at concerts: not for clout, but because capturing intense moments has become how we process them. We&#x27;ve outsourced emotional regulation to the phone, and the mere potential to share a photo now shapes how much we value the experience itself.\n\nwhen you think of why people take so many pictures and videos at concerts what do you think the reason is is it because they want to post it they want to seem cool because they&#x27;re at this show and they want people to know that i&#x27;m reading this great book called the story of your life how social media shapes the way we experience everything by katherine jesser morton it&#x27;s out later this year and she has a different reason and it feels immediately spot on so specifically for the concert she writes capturing the moment is part of how we have learned to express excitement and manage emotions that can be overwhelming the capturing of those feelings has become part of how we experience the feelings themselves the idea that you could be at a concert and you are just so overstimulated that you are attempting to like process or diffuse that or understand it by pulling out your phone and it&#x27;s this subconscious thing that it&#x27;s like attempting to help us regulate ourselves almost or to understand the moment we&#x27;re in because we&#x27;ve lost the ability to interpret things to sit in like feelings of emotional heightenedness that&#x27;s crazy and then she also says generating photographic evidence is one of the ways we manage to isolate our experiences in the torrent of immediacy that surrounds us it&#x27;s what makes things feel more real whether in the capturing or in the sharing even if we don&#x27;t share a photo we see it as a commodity that could be shared that would be received in a certain way that&#x27;s part of what determines the value of the photograph and in turn the experience so it&#x27;s like we know for a fact most people are not posting their concert footage that they take at the concert that they record the entire video of and never post because the currency is in what it how it would be or could be received if you were to post that that is enough so it&#x27;s both like how we are valuing our own experiences and lives and also how we are just understanding them processing them and our emotions in them you</details>",
    "blocks": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 1,
          "text": "Why We Film at Concerts"
        },
        {
