  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbJBpXNg4I-/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Founder Content Compass Explained</b>\n<i>The Founder Content Compass gives founders two tools: four story sources (expertise, beliefs, process, offer) and a three-layer depth drill (what happened → why it matters → why should someone else care) that turns flat posts into emotionally resonant content.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Compass direction 1 — Expertise (North): industry observations, insights, myths, recurring mistakes\n• Compass direction 2 — Beliefs (South): opinions, values, lessons that changed how you think\n• Compass direction 3 — Process (East): BTS, client transformations, case studies\n• Compass direction 4 — Offer (West): products and services you sell\n• Story layer 1 — Surface level (Too Basic): state what happened\n• Story layer 2 — Why it matters: add the real reason behind the surface fact\n• Story layer 3 — Truth (good story): the emotional core — why should someone else care\n\n💾 <i>Compact, repeatable framework for founders who know what to say but can&#x27;t make audiences feel it.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbJBpXNg4I-/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#content #founder-brand #storytelling</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Founder Content Compass Explained</b><br><i>The Founder Content Compass gives founders two tools: four story sources (expertise, beliefs, process, offer) and a three-layer depth drill (what happened → why it matters → why should someone else care) that turns flat posts into emotionally resonant content.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Compass direction 1 — Expertise (North): industry observations, insights, myths, recurring mistakes</li><li>Compass direction 2 — Beliefs (South): opinions, values, lessons that changed how you think</li><li>Compass direction 3 — Process (East): BTS, client transformations, case studies</li><li>Compass direction 4 — Offer (West): products and services you sell</li><li>Story layer 1 — Surface level (Too Basic): state what happened</li><li>Story layer 2 — Why it matters: add the real reason behind the surface fact</li><li>Story layer 3 — Truth (good story): the emotional core — why should someone else care</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Compact, repeatable framework for founders who know what to say but can&#x27;t make audiences feel it.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbJBpXNg4I-/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#content #founder-brand #storytelling</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Framework reel introducing two tools: (1) the Founder Content Compass mapping every business story to one of four directions — expertise, beliefs, process, offer — and (2) a three-layer depth drill (surface → why it matters → emotional truth) that turns ordinary founder stories into ones people connect with.\n\nThis little compass is the reason I&#x27;ve never run out of things to say about my business. Every story your business will ever tell already lives inside these four directions. You just don&#x27;t know it yet. I call it the founder content compass and it answers two questions. One, where do my stories come from? Two, how do I make people care about them? First, it&#x27;ll tell you where your stories come from. The north star is your expertise, what you know, industry observations, insights, myths, mistakes you see over and over again. Then your beliefs, your opinions, your values, the lessons that completely changed how you think. Then is your process, BTS, client transformations, case studies. And then is your offer, what you sell, your products, your services. Every story you&#x27;ll ever tell will come from one of these four directions. But here&#x27;s where most founders get stuck. Knowing what to say doesn&#x27;t mean people will care. That is why every story has three layers. What happened, why it matters and why should someone else care? Let&#x27;s say I want to tell the story of why I started my business. Surface level is I started my business because I wanted more freedom. Fine. But why did you want more freedom? Maybe because I was burnt out in my 9 to 5. Now I understand your story, but I still don&#x27;t feel it. So I ask one more time, why does that matter? Maybe because every Sunday night I&#x27;d sit on my bedroom floor dreading Monday morning, wondering, is this really going to be my life? I realized I wasn&#x27;t chasing freedom. I was trying to stop feeling trapped. That is what turns an ordinary story into the one people connect with. Most founders are stuck here, but founders building memorable brands are here. This is exactly why we are building in my 6-week challenge. Not more content, a repeatable way to talk about your business and build a brand. Comment founder and I&#x27;ll send you the details. Comment founder and I&#x27;ll send you the details.</details>",
    "blocks": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 1,
          "text": "Founder Content Compass Explained"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
