              "text": "In the spirit of becoming more curious, let's do a mind mapping of where our head was this past month. I've talked in a previous video about how at the core of building your curiosity is reflection. So this exercise is the application of that. There are no rules, but if you do want guidelines, I would start out with like a big node of an event or something you watch or read. Anything that pulled your curiosity or wherever your mind went and then branch out from that. I'm gonna make mine and then I'll show you. This is what I came up with. Let's go over it. I started here. I watched two things this past month, the drama and the violin beyond the villa. And it both reminded me of unreliable narrators. I also read the book In the Storm, which deals with social media and the lack of distance, i.e. parasociality. And obviously with social media, my relationship to it as a content creator. Have fun with this exercise. Just remember that it is for you and no one else."
