  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbTc8mytkkX/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Frontal Lobe 4-Page Journal Method</b>\n\n🪜 <b>How to</b>\n1. Page 1 — Goals: Write your goals in obsessive detail — what success looks like, what you&#x27;re working towards, what kind of life you&#x27;re building\n2. Page 2 — Reminders and Affirmations: Write what kind of person you are becoming, what motivates you, and what mindset you want to maintain\n3. Page 3 — Proof of Progress: Write what effort you made, what skill you practiced, and what you learned; track daily micro-learning progress during commutes or dead time (creator uses BeFreed for this)\n4. Page 4 — Learning Takeaways: Write the exact insight gained, how it connects to your own life, and what you will do differently going forward — be specific, not generic\n\n<i>Useful for: Anyone who wants a structured daily journaling system to gain clarity on goals, identity, progress, and learning.</i>\n\n💾 <i>A concrete 4-page daily journaling framework that integrates goal clarity, identity reinforcement, progress tracking, and learning consolidation into one structured session.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbTc8mytkkX/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#journaling #self-improvement #productivity</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Frontal Lobe 4-Page Journal Method</b><br>🪜 <b>How to</b><br><ol><li>Page 1 — Goals: Write your goals in obsessive detail — what success looks like, what you&#x27;re working towards, what kind of life you&#x27;re building</li><li>Page 2 — Reminders and Affirmations: Write what kind of person you are becoming, what motivates you, and what mindset you want to maintain</li><li>Page 3 — Proof of Progress: Write what effort you made, what skill you practiced, and what you learned; track daily micro-learning progress during commutes or dead time (creator uses BeFreed for this)</li><li>Page 4 — Learning Takeaways: Write the exact insight gained, how it connects to your own life, and what you will do differently going forward — be specific, not generic</li></ol><br><i>Useful for: Anyone who wants a structured daily journaling system to gain clarity on goals, identity, progress, and learning.</i><br>💾 <i>A concrete 4-page daily journaling framework that integrates goal clarity, identity reinforcement, progress tracking, and learning consolidation into one structured session.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbTc8mytkkX/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#journaling #self-improvement #productivity</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>A structured journaling system called the Frontal Lobe Method: Page 1 defines goals in obsessive detail, Page 2 reinforces identity and mindset via affirmations, Page 3 tracks effort and micro-learning progress (with a plug for the BeFreed app), and Page 4 captures specific insights and how they will change your actions.\n\nThis is a 10 out of 10 journaling method for gaining disgusting levels of clarity about your life. And it&#x27;s actually so fucking niche. Alright, so it&#x27;s called the frontal lobe method. Essentially there are four pages that you&#x27;re going to write. That sounds like a lot, but hear me out. The first page should be about your goals. You have to write about them in obsessive detail. What does success actually look like for you? What are you working towards? What kind of life are you trying to build? The second page is for reminders and affirmations. You&#x27;re going to remind yourself what kind of person you are becoming, what motivates you, and what mindset you want to maintain. The third page is your proof of progress page. What effort did you make? What skill did you practice? And what did you learn that could take you one step further? This is also where I track my daily micro learning progress. I always have some dead time while commuting to work, going to the gym, or heading out for a run. Instead of wasting it, I use BeFree to make the most out of it. In just 15 minutes, I can digest core ideas from actual books that relate to my goals. So instead of wasting that time scrolling, I&#x27;m learning something that could actually help me get closer to what I want. Page four is your learning takeaway page. This is where you write what you&#x27;ve gained from what you&#x27;ve been learning. What changed in the way you think? What you understand now that you didn&#x27;t understand before? How is that going to change the way you act moving forward? You have to go into detail here. Don&#x27;t just write, I learned something useful. Write down the exact insight, how it connects to your own life, and what you&#x27;re going to do differently because of it. By the end of these four pages, you know exactly what you want, who you are becoming, what you&#x27;ve done, and what you&#x27;ve learned. Comment method and I&#x27;ll send this app to you.</details>",
