  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbd_1-OtDmS/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Build DIY PR Pipeline With AI</b>\n\n🪜 <b>How to</b>\n1. Scrape a list of journalists from sites where they post live story requests\n2. Save the journalist list to a database — Airtable, Notion, Supabase, Postgres, or Google Sheets\n3. Scrape each journalist&#x27;s 10 most recent articles and store them back in the same database\n4. Run a Story Ideator AI prompt (Prompt 03): feed it the journalist&#x27;s request, profile, recent stories, founder dossier, and company news — outputs top 3 pitch ideas with headline, hook, and relevance score\n5. Run a Pitch Writer AI prompt (Prompt 05): takes request + recent stories + founder dossier and outputs a personalized 200-word email pitch\n6. Send the email; accumulate enough coverage and the Google knowledge panel appears on its own\n\n<i>Useful for: Founders who want to earn media coverage without paying a PR agency.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Breaks down a $10k PR agency workflow into a replicable AI-agent pipeline any founder can build for free.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbd_1-OtDmS/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#founder-pr #ai-agent #media-outreach</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Build DIY PR Pipeline With AI</b><br>🪜 <b>How to</b><br><ol><li>Scrape a list of journalists from sites where they post live story requests</li><li>Save the journalist list to a database — Airtable, Notion, Supabase, Postgres, or Google Sheets</li><li>Scrape each journalist&#x27;s 10 most recent articles and store them back in the same database</li><li>Run a Story Ideator AI prompt (Prompt 03): feed it the journalist&#x27;s request, profile, recent stories, founder dossier, and company news — outputs top 3 pitch ideas with headline, hook, and relevance score</li><li>Run a Pitch Writer AI prompt (Prompt 05): takes request + recent stories + founder dossier and outputs a personalized 200-word email pitch</li><li>Send the email; accumulate enough coverage and the Google knowledge panel appears on its own</li></ol><br><i>Useful for: Founders who want to earn media coverage without paying a PR agency.</i><br>💾 <i>Breaks down a $10k PR agency workflow into a replicable AI-agent pipeline any founder can build for free.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbd_1-OtDmS/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#founder-pr #ai-agent #media-outreach</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>The creator shows how to reverse-engineer a PR agency workflow using AI agents. The pipeline scrapes sites where journalists post source requests, stores them in a database (Airtable, Notion, Supabase, etc.), reads each journalist&#x27;s 10 recent articles, uses a Story Ideator prompt to generate pitch ideas, then drafts a personalized 200-word pitch email — all without paying a publicist. Enough coverage eventually triggers an organic Google knowledge panel.\n\nSomething broke when founders started buying their fame. Choose any founder. Like, search their name on Google. How did they get Google to show them as, like, a celebrity? They paid a bunch of money to one of these PR agencies&#x27; house. Can we, like, build some shit ourselves right now, dude? What do these people actually do? Apparently, it&#x27;s this. First, they make, like, a list of journalists. Give this prompt to your AI agent, and it will go and scrape all of these sites. This is where journalists post what they&#x27;re trying to write about. It should save that list of journalists to one of these databases. Next, the publicist will read their 10 previous articles. This prompt got you covered. It will scrape them and save them back to your database. Shit, we gotta come up with a story idea, right? Some idea that&#x27;s very similar to the previous stories that the journalists put out. But, like, you&#x27;re in it. And then they&#x27;ll just, like, fucking email it. Being like, yo, I read all your recent stories. I have a very similar one that you will like. This prompt will do exactly that. Eventually, somebody will probably feature you. Once you have enough coverage, that, like, panel thing just kind of appears by itself. You didn&#x27;t need to pay 10 grand for that, dude. Follow your boy instead. I&#x27;ll teach you how to build all this stuff yourself.</details>",
    "blocks": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 1,
          "text": "Build DIY PR Pipeline With AI"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 3,
          "text": "🪜 How to"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "1. "
            },
            "Scrape a list of journalists from sites where they post live story requests"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "2. "
            },
            "Save the journalist list to a database — Airtable, Notion, Supabase, Postgres, or Google Sheets"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "3. "
            },
            "Scrape each journalist's 10 most recent articles and store them back in the same database"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "4. "
            },
            "Run a Story Ideator AI prompt (Prompt 03): feed it the journalist's request, profile, recent stories, founder dossier, and company news — outputs top 3 pitch ideas with headline, hook, and relevance score"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "5. "
            },
            "Run a Pitch Writer AI prompt (Prompt 05): takes request + recent stories + founder dossier and outputs a personalized 200-word email pitch"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "6. "
            },
            "Send the email; accumulate enough coverage and the Google knowledge panel appears on its own"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "italic",
              "text": "Useful for: Founders who want to earn media coverage without paying a PR agency."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "💾 Breaks down a $10k PR agency workflow into a replicable AI-agent pipeline any founder can build for free."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "url",
              "text": "🔗 Original reel",
              "url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbd_1-OtDmS/"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "details",
          "summary": "📄 Full transcript",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The creator shows how to reverse-engineer a PR agency workflow using AI agents. The pipeline scrapes sites where journalists post source requests, stores them in a database (Airtable, Notion, Supabase, etc.), reads each journalist's 10 recent articles, uses a Story Ideator prompt to generate pitch ideas, then drafts a personalized 200-word pitch email — all without paying a publicist. Enough coverage eventually triggers an organic Google knowledge panel."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Something broke when founders started buying their fame. Choose any founder. Like, search their name on Google. How did they get Google to show them as, like, a celebrity? They paid a bunch of money to one of these PR agencies' house. Can we, like, build some shit ourselves right now, dude? What do these people actually do? Apparently, it's this. First, they make, like, a list of journalists. Give this prompt to your AI agent, and it will go and scrape all of these sites. This is where journalists post what they're trying to write about. It should save that list of journalists to one of these databases. Next, the publicist will read their 10 previous articles. This prompt got you covered. It will scrape them and save them back to your database. Shit, we gotta come up with a story idea, right? Some idea that's very similar to the previous stories that the journalists put out. But, like, you're in it. And then they'll just, like, fucking email it. Being like, yo, I read all your recent stories. I have a very similar one that you will like. This prompt will do exactly that. Eventually, somebody will probably feature you. Once you have enough coverage, that, like, panel thing just kind of appears by itself. You didn't need to pay 10 grand for that, dude. Follow your boy instead. I'll teach you how to build all this stuff yourself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "text": "#founder-pr #ai-agent #media-outreach"
        }
      ]
    },
