  "https://www.instagram.com/p/DbjniNVjWYG/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>The Addiction Storytelling Framework</b>\n<i>“The founders with the best stories win.”</i>\n\n🪜 <b>How to</b>\n1. Line 1 — The Mirror: reflect where the viewer is right now (&quot;You built a business that looks successful, but you&#x27;re still the bottleneck.&quot;)\n2. Line 2 — The Friction: name why they&#x27;re stuck\n3. Line 3 — The Realization: deliver the epiphany no one told them (&quot;The problem isn&#x27;t work ethic. It&#x27;s that you ARE the system. Replace yourself with systems, everything accelerates.&quot;)\n4. Line 4 — The Shift: show your own transformation (&quot;I went from 15-hour days to 4-hour days. Burnt out to energized. Trapped to free.&quot;)\n5. Line 5 — The Invitation: present the CTA as the natural next step (&quot;If this resonates, here&#x27;s what to do.&quot;)\n\n<i>Useful for: Founders and content creators who want to use personal storytelling to grow on social media and convert audiences into buyers.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Concise, actionable 5-part framework for turning authentic personal stories into viral content and sales, built around proven psychological principles.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DbjniNVjWYG/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#storytelling #content-creation #founder</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>The Addiction Storytelling Framework</b><br><i>“The founders with the best stories win.”</i><br>🪜 <b>How to</b><br><ol><li>Line 1 — The Mirror: reflect where the viewer is right now (&quot;You built a business that looks successful, but you&#x27;re still the bottleneck.&quot;)</li><li>Line 2 — The Friction: name why they&#x27;re stuck</li><li>Line 3 — The Realization: deliver the epiphany no one told them (&quot;The problem isn&#x27;t work ethic. It&#x27;s that you ARE the system. Replace yourself with systems, everything accelerates.&quot;)</li><li>Line 4 — The Shift: show your own transformation (&quot;I went from 15-hour days to 4-hour days. Burnt out to energized. Trapped to free.&quot;)</li><li>Line 5 — The Invitation: present the CTA as the natural next step (&quot;If this resonates, here&#x27;s what to do.&quot;)</li></ol><br><i>Useful for: Founders and content creators who want to use personal storytelling to grow on social media and convert audiences into buyers.</i><br>💾 <i>Concise, actionable 5-part framework for turning authentic personal stories into viral content and sales, built around proven psychological principles.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DbjniNVjWYG/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#storytelling #content-creation #founder</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>5-part system: (1) Make stories addictive — open a loop early using the Zeigarnik Effect and delay the answer; (2) Use storytelling as your growth funnel — attention → trust → belief → action, people remember stories 22x more than facts; (3) Your authentic story is your unfair advantage — challenges, mistakes, and hard-won systems can&#x27;t be copied; (4) Apply the Five-Line Framework (Mirror → Friction → Realization → Shift → Invitation) rooted in the Hero&#x27;s Journey; (5) Make CTAs inevitable — the story opens a loop, the lead magnet closes it.\n\n<b>Slide 1</b> — <i>Title card introducing the Addiction Framework</i>\nHow to become a storytelling genius\n(the addiction framework)\n\n<b>Slide 2</b> — <i>Hook slide with concentric circles numbered 1–6 hinting at a multi-part framework</i>\nWhat if the reason your social media isn&#x27;t growing has nothing to do with your strategy, and everything to do with the way you tell stories?\n\n<b>Slide 3</b> — <i>Author&#x27;s credibility claim and preview of the 5-part framework</i>\nI built a system that turned my stories into connections with billionaires, Fortune 500 CEOs, and millions of dollars.\n\nIt helps me engineer viral content consistently.\n\nHere&#x27;s the 5-part framework that turns any story into profit:\n\n<b>Slide 4</b> — <i>Part 1 intro — using a real video example to illustrate the Zeigarnik Effect</i>\nPart 1\nMake your stories addictive\n\nMy &quot;How to Work Less and Earn More&quot; video hit 598,000 views.\n\nIt opened with one line: &quot;If you thought of someone making $730K per month, how long would you guess they&#x27;re working?&quot;\n\nThen I held the tension and didn&#x27;t answer it for several minutes. People couldn&#x27;t click away. It&#x27;s called the Zeigarnik Effect.\n\n<b>Slide 5</b> — <i>Examples of loop-opening phrases and the neurological reason they keep audiences hooked</i>\nYour brain hates unfinished business.\n\nOpen a loop and people physically can&#x27;t leave until it closes.\n\n&quot;What I realized next surprised me&quot;\n&quot;This almost killed the business&quot;\n&quot;I didn&#x27;t understand this for years&quot;\n&quot;You wouldn&#x27;t believe what happened next&quot;\n\nThese create questions in people&#x27;s minds.\n\nTheir nervous system craves closure and can&#x27;t stop thinking about it until it&#x27;s resolved.\n\n<b>Slide 6</b> — <i>Part 2 — the four-stage storytelling funnel from scroll-stop to purchase</i>\nPart 2\nUse storytelling as your growth engine\n\nPeople remember stories 22x more than facts\nStorytelling is your fastest funnel to revenue\n\nAttention gets people to stop scrolling\nattention → trust → belief → action\nTrust makes them listen\nBelief makes them think, &quot;This could work for me.&quot;\nAction is when they buy.\n\n<b>Slide 7</b> — <i>Facts vs. Stories comparison showing how mirroring the viewer&#x27;s experience drives trust and action</i>\nMirror your viewer&#x27;s reality first.\n\nShow them you&#x27;ve been where they are.\n\nMake them feel understood through your story.\n\nThat&#x27;s how you move them from attention to action and make profits faster.\n\nFacts: &quot;At Founder OS we teach systems that help remove founders from operations&quot;\nStories: &quot;I was working 15-hour days at 22, miserable and trapped in my business. Then I discovered how to work only 4 hours a day, earning $730k/month.&quot;\n\nShow people where you were vs. where you are. Tell that story. The founders with the best stories win.\n\n<b>Slide 8</b> — <i>Part 3 — SKIMS as a case study: personal story creates a competitive moat products alone cannot</i>\nPart 3\nUse Your Story as Your Unfair Advantage\n\nLook at Kim Kardashian&#x27;s SKIMS vs every other shapewear brand.\n\nSame product. Same factories. But SKIMS crushes them.\n\nWhy? People buy into Kim&#x27;s story - her journey.\n\nHer obsession with shapewear because of the insane outfits she wears.\n\nThat&#x27;s the moat generic brands can&#x27;t copy.\n\n<b>Slide 9</b> — <i>Authenticity breakdown — what specific story material to mine and share</i>\nYour authenticity - the challenges, mistakes, systems you wish you had five years ago - that&#x27;s what sets you apart.\n\nShare the chaos that almost broke you.\n\nThe moment everything shifted.\n\nYour actual life.\n\nThose are the stories your audience needs now.\n\n<b>Slide 10</b> — <i>Part 4 intro — the Five-Line Framework is rooted in the Hero&#x27;s Journey narrative arc</i>\nPart 4\nUse The Five-Line Story Framework\n\nEvery story that makes money follows the same five-line structure:\n\nThe Hero&#x27;s Journey.\n\nStar Wars. The Matrix. Harry Potter. Ancient myths.\n\nEvery story you love follows this arc.\n\n<b>Slide 11</b> — <i>Full Five-Line Framework with labeled steps and verbatim example lines for each</i>\nMirror your viewer&#x27;s reality first.\n\nLine 1: The Mirror - Where they are right now.\n&quot;You built a business that looks successful, but you&#x27;re still the bottleneck.&quot;\n\nLine 2: The Friction - Why they&#x27;re stuck.\n&quot;You built a business that looks successful, but you&#x27;re still the bottleneck.&quot;\n\nLine 3: The Realization - The epiphany no one tells them.\n&quot;The problem isn&#x27;t work ethic. It&#x27;s that you ARE the system. Replace yourself with systems, everything accelerates.&quot;\n\nLine 4: The Shift - Your transformation.\n&quot;I went from 15-hour days to 4-hour days. Burnt out to energized. Trapped to free.&quot;\n\nLine 5: The Invitation - This is the natural next step.\n&quot;If this resonates, here&#x27;s what to do.&quot;\n\n<b>Slide 12</b> — <i>Part 5 — how to attach a CTA that feels like the story&#x27;s resolution, not a pitch</i>\nPart 5\nTurn Stories into Sales\n\nMost people make this mistake: They share a vulnerable story, then suddenly: &quot;Join my newsletter! Book a call!&quot;\n\nThat jolts people out of the story.\n\nBut a good CTA is inevitable. The natural next step.\n\nThe story opens a loop. The lead magnet closes it.</details>",
