    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>The poor man works nonstop. The rich man lives off the poor man&#x27;s labor. The soldier protects them both. The taxpayer pays the bill for all three. The bank robs all four. The lawyer stands in court for all five. The doctor sends a bill to all six. And the criminal terrifies all seven. The politician, he lives like a king off all six.</b>”\n— nedwagner\n\n<i>A quote attributed to Roman orator Cicero in 43 BC, describing how each societal class exploits or burdens the next — framed as proof that human power dynamics have never changed.</i>\n\n💾 <i>A viral societal observation with a 2000-year-old attribution — worth keeping both for the quote itself and the fact-checked note that it is a misattribution.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbdnhi8sSMe/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#cicero #society #power</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>The poor man works nonstop. The rich man lives off the poor man&#x27;s labor. The soldier protects them both. The taxpayer pays the bill for all three. The bank robs all four. The lawyer stands in court for all five. The doctor sends a bill to all six. And the criminal terrifies all seven. The politician, he lives like a king off all six.</b>”<br>— nedwagner<br><i>A quote attributed to Roman orator Cicero in 43 BC, describing how each societal class exploits or burdens the next — framed as proof that human power dynamics have never changed.</i><br>💾 <i>A viral societal observation with a 2000-year-old attribution — worth keeping both for the quote itself and the fact-checked note that it is a misattribution.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbdnhi8sSMe/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#cicero #society #power</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>A widely circulated quote credited to Cicero (43 BC) cataloguing how every societal class preys on the next, with the politician living off all. The attribution is disputed: fact-checkers at Snopes, Check Your Fact, and AAP found no trace of this text in any of Cicero&#x27;s known surviving writings.\n\nThe poor man works nonstop. The rich man lives off the poor man&#x27;s labor. The soldier protects them both. The taxpayer pays the bill for all three. The bank robs all four. The lawyer stands in court for all five. The doctor sends a bill to all six. And the criminal terrifies all seven. The politician, he lives like a king off all six. This was a quote from Cicero in 43 BC. Sounds like he wrote it just yesterday.</details>",
