        },
        {
          "type": "details",
          "summary": "📄 Full transcript",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "A widely circulated quote credited to Cicero (43 BC) cataloguing how every societal class preys on the next, with the politician living off all. The attribution is disputed: fact-checkers at Snopes, Check Your Fact, and AAP found no trace of this text in any of Cicero's known surviving writings."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The poor man works nonstop. The rich man lives off the poor man's labor. The soldier protects them both. The taxpayer pays the bill for all three. The bank robs all four. The lawyer stands in court for all five. The doctor sends a bill to all six. And the criminal terrifies all seven. The politician, he lives like a king off all six. This was a quote from Cicero in 43 BC. Sounds like he wrote it just yesterday."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "text": "#cicero #society #power"
        }
      ]
    },
    "platform": "instagram",
    "ts": "2026-08-03T23:29:02"
  },
