          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two-schedule system: batch monthly for 4x/week creators, batch weekly for 1-2x/day creators. Both rely on templates and mixing high/low-effort content. Schedule 2 batch day runs 8am–3:30pm with Poppy AI for scripting and CapCut for daily 1-hour edits."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "I create a full month of content in just one day, here is my exact schedule plus a weekly version including timestamps. This is schedule one, it's for creators who want to post four times a week, you can batch all of your content once a month. Two things make this work, the first is templates for things like scripts, captions, hooks. The second is a mix of high effort and low effort content. High effort content is things like talking to camera, low effort is things like b-roll reels with text on top. You need a mixture of both or else you're not going to finish your content for the day. Now if you're posting seven times a week or more you're going to batch weekly instead. Here's the schedule. Same principles apply, use a mixture of effort levels and use templates. The difference here is the daily editing block for anyone who's posting twice a day. In that case everything is already filmed on your batch day so every morning you're just going to spend one hour in CapCut and edit your content for that day. You're not creating from scratch every day. Or you can skip the editing entirely and use apps like these to edit for you. Save this for when you need it and all the content templates you need are inside of my content batching blueprint. Just comment blueprint and I'll send you the link."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "text": "#content-batching #scheduling #productivity"
        }
      ]
