  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbGTz3iq8fT/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Compress 12 Months Into 12 Weeks</b>\n<i>Three high-leverage habits — quarterly sprint goals, weekly reviews, and morning time blocking — can compress 12 months of progress into 12 weeks.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Set one 12-week sprint goal: pick the one thing that will change everything and give it a single 12-week window — long enough for real progress, short enough to stay locked in\n• Do a 15-minute Sunday weekly review: ask what worked, what didn&#x27;t, and what&#x27;s next — you can&#x27;t improve what you don&#x27;t measure\n• Time-block your hardest task first thing in the morning, when your prefrontal cortex is freshest, before the noise kicks in\n\n💾 <i>Compact, immediately actionable framework for accelerating goal achievement using just three repeatable weekly and quarterly habits.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbGTz3iq8fT/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#productivity #goal-setting #time-blocking</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Compress 12 Months Into 12 Weeks</b><br><i>Three high-leverage habits — quarterly sprint goals, weekly reviews, and morning time blocking — can compress 12 months of progress into 12 weeks.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Set one 12-week sprint goal: pick the one thing that will change everything and give it a single 12-week window — long enough for real progress, short enough to stay locked in</li><li>Do a 15-minute Sunday weekly review: ask what worked, what didn&#x27;t, and what&#x27;s next — you can&#x27;t improve what you don&#x27;t measure</li><li>Time-block your hardest task first thing in the morning, when your prefrontal cortex is freshest, before the noise kicks in</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Compact, immediately actionable framework for accelerating goal achievement using just three repeatable weekly and quarterly habits.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbGTz3iq8fT/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#productivity #goal-setting #time-blocking</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Three-tip productivity framework: set one 12-week goal, do a 15-min Sunday review (what worked / didn&#x27;t / what&#x27;s next), and time-block hard tasks first in the morning when the brain is sharpest.\n\n10 out of 10 ways to get ahead in 12 weeks. That takes most people 12 months. Most people set goals once a year and wonder why they never hit them. Here&#x27;s how to compress 12 months into 12 weeks. Number one, quarterly sprint goals. Pick one thing that will change everything and give it 12 weeks. Long enough to make real progress but short enough to stay locked in. Number two, weekly reviews. Every Sunday ask yourself what worked, what didn&#x27;t and what&#x27;s next. Takes 15 minutes and you can improve what you don&#x27;t measure. Number three, time blocking. Your brain can&#x27;t multitask. The best thing you can do is plan your hardest task first thing in the morning. Your prefrontal cortex is freshest in the morning so use it properly before the noise kicks in. Comment systems and I&#x27;ll send you the exact journal I use to track all of this.</details>",
