  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Da4N-KVxRIv/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Warren Buffett&#x27;s 5/25 Focus Rule</b>\n<i>Use Warren Buffett&#x27;s 5/25 rule to cut goal overwhelm: your top 5 get full attention, everything else goes on an &quot;avoid at all costs&quot; list until you find success there.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Chasing too many goals simultaneously leads to exhaustion and loss of joy in your work\n• Unfinished pursuits are not wasted — but they go nowhere without real focus\n• The avoid-at-all-costs list is temporary, not permanent — revisit once you&#x27;ve made progress on your top 5\n\n💾 <i>A concrete, repeatable framework for ruthless prioritization that forces you to name what to stop pursuing, not just what to start.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Da4N-KVxRIv/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#focus #prioritization #goals</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Warren Buffett&#x27;s 5/25 Focus Rule</b><br><i>Use Warren Buffett&#x27;s 5/25 rule to cut goal overwhelm: your top 5 get full attention, everything else goes on an &quot;avoid at all costs&quot; list until you find success there.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Chasing too many goals simultaneously leads to exhaustion and loss of joy in your work</li><li>Unfinished pursuits are not wasted — but they go nowhere without real focus</li><li>The avoid-at-all-costs list is temporary, not permanent — revisit once you&#x27;ve made progress on your top 5</li></ul><br>💾 <i>A concrete, repeatable framework for ruthless prioritization that forces you to name what to stop pursuing, not just what to start.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Da4N-KVxRIv/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#focus #prioritization #goals</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Feeling overwhelmed by too many parallel pursuits, the creator does a hard reset using Buffett&#x27;s Two-List method — write 25 goals, circle the top 5, actively avoid the remaining 20 until the top 5 show progress.\n\nthere are only five months left in the year so if you&#x27;re looking at your mountain of goals and feeling like it&#x27;s too late to try i&#x27;m right there with you i&#x27;m the person with 47 tabs open because i want to learn everything last fall i was obsessed with generative ai last month i wanted to learn videography but life got in the way i also thought about expanding my e-com agency but didn&#x27;t this wasn&#x27;t time wasted but these things went nowhere a mentor once told me if you try to catch two rabbits at once you&#x27;ll eventually lose both right now it feels like i&#x27;m trying to catch seven i&#x27;m exhausted and i&#x27;m losing the joy in my work so i&#x27;m doing a hard reset for the rest of the year i found a great post by writer sam ringo on warren buffett&#x27;s five out of 25 rule it&#x27;s brutal but in the best way so i&#x27;m putting it to work first write down 25 things you want to do most then circle your top five everything not circled becomes your avoid at all costs list and not forever just until you find some success in your top five it&#x27;s simple but it&#x27;s actually hard to live by so i&#x27;ll be sharing how i&#x27;m turning it into a game plan in part two tomorrow if you want to do it with me comment reset and i&#x27;ll send you the exact file i use to narrow my 25 down to five</details>",
    "blocks": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 1,
          "text": "Warren Buffett's 5/25 Focus Rule"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "italic",
              "text": "Use Warren Buffett's 5/25 rule to cut goal overwhelm: your top 5 get full attention, everything else goes on an \"avoid at all costs\" list until you find success there."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 3,
          "text": "🔑 Key points"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Chasing too many goals simultaneously leads to exhaustion and loss of joy in your work"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Unfinished pursuits are not wasted — but they go nowhere without real focus"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The avoid-at-all-costs list is temporary, not permanent — revisit once you've made progress on your top 5"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "💾 A concrete, repeatable framework for ruthless prioritization that forces you to name what to stop pursuing, not just what to start."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "url",
              "text": "🔗 Original reel",
              "url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Da4N-KVxRIv/"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "details",
          "summary": "📄 Full transcript",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Feeling overwhelmed by too many parallel pursuits, the creator does a hard reset using Buffett's Two-List method — write 25 goals, circle the top 5, actively avoid the remaining 20 until the top 5 show progress."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "there are only five months left in the year so if you're looking at your mountain of goals and feeling like it's too late to try i'm right there with you i'm the person with 47 tabs open because i want to learn everything last fall i was obsessed with generative ai last month i wanted to learn videography but life got in the way i also thought about expanding my e-com agency but didn't this wasn't time wasted but these things went nowhere a mentor once told me if you try to catch two rabbits at once you'll eventually lose both right now it feels like i'm trying to catch seven i'm exhausted and i'm losing the joy in my work so i'm doing a hard reset for the rest of the year i found a great post by writer sam ringo on warren buffett's five out of 25 rule it's brutal but in the best way so i'm putting it to work first write down 25 things you want to do most then circle your top five everything not circled becomes your avoid at all costs list and not forever just until you find some success in your top five it's simple but it's actually hard to live by so i'll be sharing how i'm turning it into a game plan in part two tomorrow if you want to do it with me comment reset and i'll send you the exact file i use to narrow my 25 down to five"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "text": "#focus #prioritization #goals"
        }
      ]
    },
