    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>I am already enough. So let&#x27;s go use that enoughness to do something incredible with the limited time that I have been given.</b>”\n— diewithoutregretss\n\n<i>Most overachievers are driven by a subconscious fear that ties their self-worth to achievement, and the antidote is shifting from that fear (dirty fuel) to a place of already feeling enough (clean fuel).</i>\n💡 <b>You can&#x27;t think your way into clean fuel — the subconscious beliefs driving dirty fuel were formed emotionally and must be rewired the same way.</b>\n\n💾 <i>Names a concrete psychological pattern (dirty fuel) that drives high achievers and offers a reframe (clean fuel) grounded in subconscious belief work.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db0RNcwoK8d/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#overachiever #self-worth #motivation</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>I am already enough. So let&#x27;s go use that enoughness to do something incredible with the limited time that I have been given.</b>”<br>— diewithoutregretss<br><i>Most overachievers are driven by a subconscious fear that ties their self-worth to achievement, and the antidote is shifting from that fear (dirty fuel) to a place of already feeling enough (clean fuel).</i><br>💡 <b>You can&#x27;t think your way into clean fuel — the subconscious beliefs driving dirty fuel were formed emotionally and must be rewired the same way.</b><br>💾 <i>Names a concrete psychological pattern (dirty fuel) that drives high achievers and offers a reframe (clean fuel) grounded in subconscious belief work.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db0RNcwoK8d/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#overachiever #self-worth #motivation</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Dirty fuel is fear-driven achievement where self-worth depends on results; clean fuel is acting from wholeness. The shift requires emotional rewiring of subconscious beliefs, not just mindset shifts.\n\nI have a deep belief that if you&#x27;re an overachiever, the quality of your life is determined by how you answer the following question. What&#x27;s actually driving you? Because I think most overachievers are being driven by something that they don&#x27;t fully understand. I call it dirty fuel. Dirty fuel is the chip on your shoulder. It&#x27;s the voice that says, Fuck you, I will prove you wrong. It&#x27;s powerful. In fact, it&#x27;s usually what creates ambitious people in the first place. But it comes with a cost. Because it&#x27;s kind of like putting rocket fuel in a car engine. The acceleration is incredible, but slowly the engine pays the price. Because underneath all of the work ethic and the discipline, that fuel is fear. Usually a subconscious fear that says, If I don&#x27;t achieve X, then I am not worthy of Y. X might be money, status, recognition, success. And Y is usually something much deeper, like love, respect, belonging, peace. And when your self-worth becomes tied to your achievement, the stakes become impossibly fucking high. Setbacks feel devastating. Switching off feels uncomfortable. Rest feels lazy. Nothing ever quite feels enough. Because you&#x27;re not just trying to build something, You&#x27;re trying to outrun something. But there is some good news. And the good news is there is another fuel source you can tap into if you so wish to. A fuel source that I refer to as clean fuel. Clean fuel, in a sentence, is this. I am already enough. So let&#x27;s go use that enoughness to do something incredible with the limited time that I have been given. Clean fuel is this sweet cocktail of play, curiosity, service, mastery, and a genuine love of the game. You can move as fast as you like, but now it comes from wholeness, not lack. But here is the rather annoying part. You can&#x27;t just think your way into clean fuel. The beliefs that formed your dirty fuel weren&#x27;t formed logically. They were formed emotionally, usually through uncomfortable childhood experiences. Those experiences created subconscious beliefs about who you are, what you&#x27;re worth, and what you need to do to feel enough. Those beliefs are your dirty fuel. And it is only on the other side of bringing those into awareness, and doing the work to rewire them, that you can tap into that clean fuel. Now a quick shameless plug. In my one-to-one coaching, I actually help overachievers uncover and reprogram those very subconscious beliefs, so that they can start operating from clean fuel. And I do so using hypnotherapy. I&#x27;m about to open a little bit more space, so if you want to know more, you can DM me the words clean fuel, and I&#x27;ll send you more details.</details>",
