          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "details",
          "summary": "📄 Full transcript",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Four practical drills to consciously develop viral intuition — from guessing metrics and comment sections to using an AI content tool (Stanley) with a detailed 5-section breakdown prompt, and training the Instagram algorithm to surface only high-performing videos."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "10 out of 10 ways to build disgustingly strong viral sense, but it gets increasingly more niche. When doom scrolling, hide the engagement metrics of a video and guess how many likes and views that video has in order to consciously assess its viral quality. When watching a video that is a high ratio of comments, try and guess what people are commenting about in the comment section before opening it up in order to force yourself to identify what element in the video is the most interesting to the average viewer. When coming across a viral video that you are unsure why performed well but want to use as inspiration, copy its link and paste it into an AI built for content like Stanley, then ask it to transcribe the video and psychologically break down and analyze why the video performed well using this prompt. If you want the prompt guide, just comment guide and I'll send it over. And finally, when assessing your feed and explore page, actively engage with viral videos only by liking, commenting and clicking interested and don't engage with non-viral videos. This forces your algorithm to only show you viral videos and if you watch viral videos long enough, your viral sense will develop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
