  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db25h_xPKie/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Claude /watch-video Skill</b>\n\n🪜 <b>How to</b>\n1. Add the marketplace inside Claude Code: /plugin marketplace add coreyhaines31/makerskills\n2. Install the skill: /plugin install watch-video\n3. Run /watch-video [video URL] — append the word &#x27;visual&#x27; to enable frame analysis\n\n<i>Useful for: Anyone with a backlog of webinars, client Looms, or tutorials they want turned into structured, searchable notes automatically.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Free, two-command Claude Code skill that converts any YouTube, Loom, Vimeo, or Zoom recording into a structured searchable note — eliminates the video backlog problem.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db25h_xPKie/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#claude-code #ai-tools #video</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Claude /watch-video Skill</b><br>🪜 <b>How to</b><br><ol><li>Add the marketplace inside Claude Code: /plugin marketplace add coreyhaines31/makerskills</li><li>Install the skill: /plugin install watch-video</li><li>Run /watch-video [video URL] — append the word &#x27;visual&#x27; to enable frame analysis</li></ol><br><i>Useful for: Anyone with a backlog of webinars, client Looms, or tutorials they want turned into structured, searchable notes automatically.</i><br>💾 <i>Free, two-command Claude Code skill that converts any YouTube, Loom, Vimeo, or Zoom recording into a structured searchable note — eliminates the video backlog problem.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db25h_xPKie/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#claude-code #ai-tools #video</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>The /watch-video Claude Code skill transcribes video, captures frames at key moments, and files organized notes. Install from Corey Haines&#x27; open-source makerskills repo in two commands. Add &#x27;visual&#x27; after the URL to enable frame analysis; omit for faster transcript-only mode.\n\nClaude has a hidden skill that watches videos for you. It&#x27;s called watch video, and it works with YouTube, Loom, Vimeo, and even Zoom recording sitting on your laptop. All right, so here&#x27;s what it does. It transcribes the whole video. It pulls still frames at the key moments. It writes notes on what&#x27;s actually on screen, not just what&#x27;s said. Then it files the whole thing into an organized folder so you can search later. Setting it up takes two commands inside of Claude code. First, add the marketplace. That&#x27;s just the GitHub repo it lives in. Second, install the plugin. Now simply paste any video link like this, slash watch video, add the link, then the word visual. That last word sets the depth. Leave it off and you get the transcript only, which is faster. But when you add visual, Claude actually looks at the frames. It&#x27;s one of 15 free skills in this pack, and the whole thing is open source. If you want my full setup guide for this, comment, watch, and I&#x27;ll send it across.</details>",
    "blocks": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 1,
          "text": "Claude /watch-video Skill"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 3,
          "text": "🪜 How to"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "1. "
            },
            "Add the marketplace inside Claude Code: /plugin marketplace add coreyhaines31/makerskills"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "2. "
            },
            "Install the skill: /plugin install watch-video"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "bold",
              "text": "3. "
            },
            "Run /watch-video [video URL] — append the word 'visual' to enable frame analysis"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "italic",
              "text": "Useful for: Anyone with a backlog of webinars, client Looms, or tutorials they want turned into structured, searchable notes automatically."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "💾 Free, two-command Claude Code skill that converts any YouTube, Loom, Vimeo, or Zoom recording into a structured searchable note — eliminates the video backlog problem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "divider"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": [
            {
              "type": "url",
              "text": "🔗 Original reel",
              "url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db25h_xPKie/"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "details",
          "summary": "📄 Full transcript",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The /watch-video Claude Code skill transcribes video, captures frames at key moments, and files organized notes. Install from Corey Haines' open-source makerskills repo in two commands. Add 'visual' after the URL to enable frame analysis; omit for faster transcript-only mode."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Claude has a hidden skill that watches videos for you. It's called watch video, and it works with YouTube, Loom, Vimeo, and even Zoom recording sitting on your laptop. All right, so here's what it does. It transcribes the whole video. It pulls still frames at the key moments. It writes notes on what's actually on screen, not just what's said. Then it files the whole thing into an organized folder so you can search later. Setting it up takes two commands inside of Claude code. First, add the marketplace. That's just the GitHub repo it lives in. Second, install the plugin. Now simply paste any video link like this, slash watch video, add the link, then the word visual. That last word sets the depth. Leave it off and you get the transcript only, which is faster. But when you add visual, Claude actually looks at the frames. It's one of 15 free skills in this pack, and the whole thing is open source. If you want my full setup guide for this, comment, watch, and I'll send it across."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "text": "#claude-code #ai-tools #video"
        }
      ]
    },
