  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db9KpsTxuT-/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>5 Ways to Be Great Creator</b>\n<i>Five concrete habits that separate great content creators from average ones, from a creator with 1.3M followers.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Save outlier reels from your favorite creators to study what breaks patterns.\n• When a movie, show, or event goes viral, figure out how to link that topic to your niche.\n• Entertain and inspire first before you educate.\n• Take currently viral formats and make them more authentically yours.\n• Don&#x27;t care when a video flops — it&#x27;s evidence you&#x27;re trying and experimenting.\n\n💾 <i>Practical creator mindset checklist from a 1.3M-follower creator — five habits worth internalizing for content strategy.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db9KpsTxuT-/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#content-creation #creator-mindset #growth</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>5 Ways to Be Great Creator</b><br><i>Five concrete habits that separate great content creators from average ones, from a creator with 1.3M followers.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Save outlier reels from your favorite creators to study what breaks patterns.</li><li>When a movie, show, or event goes viral, figure out how to link that topic to your niche.</li><li>Entertain and inspire first before you educate.</li><li>Take currently viral formats and make them more authentically yours.</li><li>Don&#x27;t care when a video flops — it&#x27;s evidence you&#x27;re trying and experimenting.</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Practical creator mindset checklist from a 1.3M-follower creator — five habits worth internalizing for content strategy.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db9KpsTxuT-/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#content-creation #creator-mindset #growth</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Five actionable habits for content creators: save and study outlier reels, newsjack viral moments by linking them to your niche, entertain before you educate, remix viral formats into your own style, and treat flopped videos as proof you&#x27;re experimenting.\n\n10 out of 10 ways to become a disgustingly good content creator. You save the outlier reels of your favorite creator. When a movie, show, or event goes viral, you figure out how you can take that topic and link it to something that you enjoy talking about. You entertain and inspire first before you educate. You take currently viral formats and turn them into something that&#x27;s more you. And you don&#x27;t care when a video flops because that is evidence that you are trying and experimenting. I make thousands and thousands of dollars a month just doing content creation. So if you want to learn how, I have a couple of videos on my page explaining how you can start.</details>",
    "blocks": {
      "blocks": [
