  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbEu_wDpNL0/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Three Hacks to Fix Attention Span</b>\n<i>Three science-backed micro-habits — verbally labeling distraction urges, glancing at greenery for 40 seconds, and removing your phone from the room — measurably restore and protect attention span.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Name the distraction urge out loud (&#x27;distraction impulse&#x27;) — verbally labeling it reactivates the prefrontal cortex and interrupts the impulse\n• A 40-second glance at greenery resets sustained attention — staring out a window at grass or trees is enough\n• Phone must be in another room — even face-down on your desk it silently drains focus because part of your brain is actively working to resist looking at it\n\n💾 <i>Three immediately actionable, science-backed micro-habits that restore attention without apps or timers.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbEu_wDpNL0/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#attention #focus #neuroscience</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Three Hacks to Fix Attention Span</b><br><i>Three science-backed micro-habits — verbally labeling distraction urges, glancing at greenery for 40 seconds, and removing your phone from the room — measurably restore and protect attention span.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Name the distraction urge out loud (&#x27;distraction impulse&#x27;) — verbally labeling it reactivates the prefrontal cortex and interrupts the impulse</li><li>A 40-second glance at greenery resets sustained attention — staring out a window at grass or trees is enough</li><li>Phone must be in another room — even face-down on your desk it silently drains focus because part of your brain is actively working to resist looking at it</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Three immediately actionable, science-backed micro-habits that restore attention without apps or timers.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbEu_wDpNL0/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#attention #focus #neuroscience</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>bitterbuilds shares three unconventional attention hacks grounded in neuroscience, sourced from a Yana Yuhai Substack article (mindbox, Jun 2025): verbally name the distraction urge to interrupt it, take a 40-second nature glance per a 2015 University of Melbourne study, and physically remove your phone because even face-down on a desk it silently taxes your attention.\n\nThe fastest way to get ahead of everyone your age is to start attention span maxing. And there are three disgustingly easy ways to bring back your attention. And no, I&#x27;m not just going to tell you to use a study timer. These tips are niche and science-based. Number one, name the impulse. Whenever you feel the urge to switch tasks or check your phone, pause and label it by saying distraction impulse out loud. This is going to reactivate your prefrontal cortex. Number two, a 40-second glance at greenery resets sustained attention. Literally just stare outside your window to fix your attention span. And number three, put the phone in the other room. Even if your phone is face down on your desk, it still drains your attention because part of your brain is actively working not to look at it. Follow for more tips.</details>",
