    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>5 High-ROI Hobbies in Your 20s</b>\n<i>“You can have the money, the fitness, the success, but it doesn&#x27;t mean anything if you don&#x27;t know what you&#x27;re building them for.”</i>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n<i>Not clear from the Reel.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Concise, practical list of five high-leverage habits to build in your 20s — fitness, creation, reading, investing, and purpose — with a strong closing line on knowing what you&#x27;re building toward.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db3WYRPRXl0/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#habits #self-improvement #20s</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>5 High-ROI Hobbies in Your 20s</b><br><i>“You can have the money, the fitness, the success, but it doesn&#x27;t mean anything if you don&#x27;t know what you&#x27;re building them for.”</i><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li><i>Not clear from the Reel.</i></li></ol><br>💾 <i>Concise, practical list of five high-leverage habits to build in your 20s — fitness, creation, reading, investing, and purpose — with a strong closing line on knowing what you&#x27;re building toward.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db3WYRPRXl0/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#habits #self-improvement #20s</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Five hobbies to start in your 20s: (1) a combat sport for fitness and composure under pressure, (2) creating — writing, videos, business, music — to stay mentally active, (3) reading to absorb decades of others&#x27; experience cheaply, (4) investing in your body, skills, relationships, and eventually money since the best returns compound, and (5) prayer to get quiet, find your calling, and decide what kind of person you want to become.\n\nFive highest return on investment hobbies to start in your 20s. Learn some form of fighting, boxing, wrestling, jujitsu, Muay Thai. Just pick one and train it. It keeps you in shape, teaches you to stay calm under pressure, and now you have the ability to protect your family and your boys if you ever get jumped. Go create something, write, make videos, build a business, make music. I don&#x27;t care, even go play a video game. Anything that forces you to actually think instead of doom scroll. Number three, go read. Most people stop learning once school ends. Read about things you&#x27;re interested in. Psychology, history, business, whatever. You can learn decades of someone else&#x27;s experience for the price of a book. Number four, invest. Invest time into your body, your skills, your relationships. If you have money left over after the essentials, learn how to invest that too. The best investments don&#x27;t just pay you once, they compound. And lastly, prayer. Take time to get quiet. Ask God for guidance. Figure out what you believe, what your calling is, and what kind of person you want to become. You can have the money, the fitness, the success, but it doesn&#x27;t mean anything. If you don&#x27;t know what you&#x27;re building them for.</details>",
    "blocks": {
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "size": 1,
          "text": "5 High-ROI Hobbies in Your 20s"
        },
