    "digest": "<b>10 Levels of Fake Progress</b>\n<i>Consuming advice, taking notes, buying books, and building routines are all fake progress — they substitute the feeling of doing for actually doing.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• 1. Saving the video — you just built a graveyard for advice\n• 2. Watching in 2x speed — now you&#x27;re procrastinating efficiently\n• 3. Taking notes — if nothing changes after, that&#x27;s just handwriting\n• 4. Buying a book — the book is not a transformation, it&#x27;s the receipt\n• 5. Building the perfect routine — most guys just need to obey the one they already had\n• 6. Telling your friends your goals — that little dopamine hit is your brain pretending you already did it\n• 7. Watching discipline content while your room is disgusting — the tutorial&#x27;s on the floor\n• 8. Optimizing your setup — your life needs evidence, not another desk light\n• 9. Waiting for a fresh start (Monday, next month, next semester) — addicted to a new checkpoint\n• 10. Knowing exactly what to do and never doing it — that&#x27;s the final boss\n\n💾 <i>A clean, memorable breakdown of every fake-progress trap with a single concrete rule to break the cycle.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYZDUC0t2b5/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#fake-progress #discipline #productivity</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>10 Levels of Fake Progress</b><br><i>Consuming advice, taking notes, buying books, and building routines are all fake progress — they substitute the feeling of doing for actually doing.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>1. Saving the video — you just built a graveyard for advice</li><li>2. Watching in 2x speed — now you&#x27;re procrastinating efficiently</li><li>3. Taking notes — if nothing changes after, that&#x27;s just handwriting</li><li>4. Buying a book — the book is not a transformation, it&#x27;s the receipt</li><li>5. Building the perfect routine — most guys just need to obey the one they already had</li><li>6. Telling your friends your goals — that little dopamine hit is your brain pretending you already did it</li><li>7. Watching discipline content while your room is disgusting — the tutorial&#x27;s on the floor</li><li>8. Optimizing your setup — your life needs evidence, not another desk light</li><li>9. Waiting for a fresh start (Monday, next month, next semester) — addicted to a new checkpoint</li><li>10. Knowing exactly what to do and never doing it — that&#x27;s the final boss</li></ul><br>💾 <i>A clean, memorable breakdown of every fake-progress trap with a single concrete rule to break the cycle.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DYZDUC0t2b5/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#fake-progress #discipline #productivity</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>10 numbered fake-progress traps with sharp one-liners, ending with a single rule: proof before input — finish one real task (workout, assignment, sales message, hard task) before consuming more advice.</details>",
