  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbI3xSjTfGI/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>High Performers Detach From the Result</b>\n<i>High performers don&#x27;t procrastinate because they&#x27;ve detached from the outcome — procrastination is an attachment problem, not a discipline problem.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• High performers &#x27;don&#x27;t give a shit about the output&#x27; — they focus on the process, not the result.\n• Procrastination is an attachment problem, not a discipline problem.\n• Detaching from the result removes the fear that stops people before they even start.\n• High performers aren&#x27;t fearless — they&#x27;ve just stopped letting the output define who they are.\n\n💾 <i>Reframes procrastination as an attachment problem rather than a discipline failure — a concrete mental model shift backed by the flow state concept.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbI3xSjTfGI/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#procrastination #detachment #flow</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>High Performers Detach From the Result</b><br><i>High performers don&#x27;t procrastinate because they&#x27;ve detached from the outcome — procrastination is an attachment problem, not a discipline problem.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>High performers &#x27;don&#x27;t give a shit about the output&#x27; — they focus on the process, not the result.</li><li>Procrastination is an attachment problem, not a discipline problem.</li><li>Detaching from the result removes the fear that stops people before they even start.</li><li>High performers aren&#x27;t fearless — they&#x27;ve just stopped letting the output define who they are.</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Reframes procrastination as an attachment problem rather than a discipline failure — a concrete mental model shift backed by the flow state concept.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbI3xSjTfGI/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#procrastination #detachment #flow</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Procrastination is not a discipline problem — it&#x27;s an attachment problem. When you fear how the result defines you, you can&#x27;t start. High performers detach from the output entirely, removing that fear. The fix: stop letting results define who you are, and just take the shot.</details>",
