  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcAKI4VsESf/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>Be soooo obsessed with the experience and the journey that the outcome is just a byproduct.</b>”\n— Saba\n\n<i>As a recovering perfectionist, Saba reflects on how we refuse to begin things until we know they&#x27;ll succeed — making a guaranteed outcome a condition for participation — and argues that letting go of that expectation is what actually frees you to enjoy the process.</i>\n💡 <b>Stop making success a condition for starting; let the outcome be a byproduct of showing up for the experience.</b>\n\n💾 <i>Sharp, personal framing of outcome-detachment that goes beyond generic &quot;enjoy the journey&quot; advice — the recovering-perfectionist angle makes it land differently.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcAKI4VsESf/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#perfectionism #letting-go #process</i>",
