    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>3 Books to Understand Venture Capital</b>\n<i>“It&#x27;s the closest thing to sitting in the actual room and understanding how the best investors think.”</i>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.hup.harvard.edu/books/9780674988002\">VC: An American History</a> — Tom Nicholas\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/18050143-zero-to-one\">Zero to One: Notes on Startups, or How to Build the Future</a> — Peter Thiel\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/58009109-the-power-law\">The Power Law: Venture Capital and the Making of the New Future</a> — Sebastian Mallaby\n✅ <a href=\"https://sequoiacap.com/\">Sequoia Capital</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.kleinerperkins.com/\">Kleiner Perkins</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://www.accel.com/\">Accel</a>\n✅ <a href=\"https://visionfund.com/\">SoftBank Vision Fund</a>\n\n💾 <i>Curated VC reading list from someone who worked in the industry, covering the full arc: history from whaling ships, startup mindset from Thiel, and insider access to the math behind top funds.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Db7efDgAO2h/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#venture-capital #books #startup</i>",
