    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Skills Learned vs Scroll Time</b>\n<i>The hours spent scrolling each month are enough to learn real skills — Rubik&#x27;s cube at 30 hrs, world capitals at 90, constellations at 150, hieroglyphics at 240.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• 30 hours/month scrolling → enough to learn to solve a Rubik&#x27;s cube\n• 90 hours/month scrolling → enough to learn every country&#x27;s capital (Quizlet, 198 flashcards)\n• 150 hours/month scrolling → enough to learn astronomy / star constellations (at ~5 hours/week)\n• 240 hours/month scrolling → enough time to start understanding hieroglyphics\n\n💾 <i>Concrete opportunity-cost benchmarks make wasted scroll time tangible and actionable.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZs7YwWy_J9/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#screen-time #learning #productivity</i>",
