  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaHOAi-Atr_/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>Athletic and Aesthetic Full Masterclass</b>\n\n🪜 <b>How to</b>\n1. NUTRITION — Find maintenance: track food for 3–7 days and take the weekly average.\n2. NUTRITION — Decide goal: fat loss if abs aren&#x27;t visible; muscle gain if already lean.\n3. NUTRITION — Set weekly calorie target at ±10% of maintenance (deficit for cut, surplus for muscle).\n4. NUTRITION — Training days: protein 1g/lb BW, fats 0.6–1.0 g/kg BW (low end on cut, high end on bulk), carbs fill the rest.\n5. NUTRITION — Non-training days: drop calories 10–20%, cut carbs in half, fill remainder with fats.\n6. TRAINING — Start every session with some combination of plyometrics, sprinting, and lifting.\n7. TRAINING — Lift close to failure: 1–3 sets per exercise, 5–15 reps.\n8. TRAINING — Cover these movement patterns each session: squat, hinge, horizontal push, horizontal pull, vertical push, vertical pull, arms/laterals/leg extensions/leg curls.\n9. TRAINING — Add conditioning 1–2 times per week for an unlimited gas tank.\n10. TRACKING — Weigh yourself daily and take progress photos every week to adjust.\n\n<i>Useful for: Anyone who wants to build an aesthetic physique while staying fast, strong, and conditioned — not just big.</i>\n\n💾 <i>Complete system that makes you both jacked and athletic — covers the exact nutrition cycling protocol and training template in one short video.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaHOAi-Atr_/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#fitness #nutrition #training</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>Athletic and Aesthetic Full Masterclass</b><br>🪜 <b>How to</b><br><ol><li>NUTRITION — Find maintenance: track food for 3–7 days and take the weekly average.</li><li>NUTRITION — Decide goal: fat loss if abs aren&#x27;t visible; muscle gain if already lean.</li><li>NUTRITION — Set weekly calorie target at ±10% of maintenance (deficit for cut, surplus for muscle).</li><li>NUTRITION — Training days: protein 1g/lb BW, fats 0.6–1.0 g/kg BW (low end on cut, high end on bulk), carbs fill the rest.</li><li>NUTRITION — Non-training days: drop calories 10–20%, cut carbs in half, fill remainder with fats.</li><li>TRAINING — Start every session with some combination of plyometrics, sprinting, and lifting.</li><li>TRAINING — Lift close to failure: 1–3 sets per exercise, 5–15 reps.</li><li>TRAINING — Cover these movement patterns each session: squat, hinge, horizontal push, horizontal pull, vertical push, vertical pull, arms/laterals/leg extensions/leg curls.</li><li>TRAINING — Add conditioning 1–2 times per week for an unlimited gas tank.</li><li>TRACKING — Weigh yourself daily and take progress photos every week to adjust.</li></ol><br><i>Useful for: Anyone who wants to build an aesthetic physique while staying fast, strong, and conditioned — not just big.</i><br>💾 <i>Complete system that makes you both jacked and athletic — covers the exact nutrition cycling protocol and training template in one short video.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaHOAi-Atr_/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#fitness #nutrition #training</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Two-part protocol: cycle calories/carbs between training days (high carb, ~maintenance+10%) and non-training days (carbs halved, calories 10–20% lower), with protein at 1g/lb BW throughout. Training: start sessions with plyometrics/sprints, lift close to failure in 1–3 sets of 5–15 reps across all major movement patterns, plus conditioning 1–2x/week. Track daily weight and weekly photos.</details>",
