    "digest": "<b>Replace Screen Time with Finance Skills</b>\n<i>Replacing daily screen time with deliberate practice of four finance skills — Excel, 10-K reading, Mandarin, and negotiation — compounds into a career-defining edge on Wall Street.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• 1 hr/day → master Excel keyboard-only: build a three-statement model from a blank sheet and be the one who structures the deal\n• 3 hrs/day → read a 10-K like a menu: spot footnotes, off-balance sheet obligations, and MD&amp;A nuances that 100 analysts scroll past\n• 5 hrs/day → reach Mandarin fluency: sit across from sovereign wealth funds and close deals while competitors wait for a translator\n• 8 hrs/day → master negotiation: know the other side&#x27;s number before they say it — requires merger modeling under pressure, covenant analysis, comps and precedent transactions, credit and counterparty risk\n\n💾 <i>Concrete daily-hour benchmarks for four high-leverage finance skills — more specific than generic Wall Street career advice and doubles as a self-study roadmap.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbjfE6khVJz/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#finance #career #skill-building</i>",
