    "digest": "<b>10 Habits to Replace Doomscrolling</b>\n<i>Replace the scrolling urge with a competing physical or social action that occupies the same hand and same moment.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Do 20 push-ups the moment you feel the urge to scroll — phone stays down until the set is finished.\n• Call someone instead of texting — voice only, no typing, same conversation you&#x27;d have had in the app.\n• Take a walk after dinner — outside, no destination, 15 minutes.\n• Clear one physical drawer or folder you&#x27;ve been avoiding — not a digital one.\n• Read two pages of a book the moment you reach for your phone — same hand, different object.\n• Practice a skill for 10 minutes instead of watching someone else do it — your hands on the instrument, not your eyes on the feed.\n• Sit outside for two minutes before going back indoors — nothing in your hands, nothing playing, just sit.\n\n💾 <i>Concrete, immediately executable alternatives for the exact moment the scrolling urge hits, framed as habit replacements rather than willpower.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DaGeW4CyyLo/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#doomscrolling #habits #discipline</i>",
