    "digest": "<b>10 Sports Every Man Should Try</b>\n<i>“A dangerous man is comfortable in every environment.”</i>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n<i>Not clear from the Reel.</i>\n\n💾 <i>A ranked list of physical disciplines with sharp one-line rationale for each, useful for deciding what to train next.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZS0n_TNrLH/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#discipline #masculinity #sports</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>10 Sports Every Man Should Try</b><br><i>“A dangerous man is comfortable in every environment.”</i><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li><i>Not clear from the Reel.</i></li></ol><br>💾 <i>A ranked list of physical disciplines with sharp one-line rationale for each, useful for deciding what to train next.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZS0n_TNrLH/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#discipline #masculinity #sports</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>herman.1ind lists 10 sports in increasing order of niche-ness, each framed around a masculine ideal: physical capability, mental toughness, comfort in dangerous environments, and mastery of self.\n\n10 sports every man should try, but they get progressively more niche. Weightlifting. Build the body first. Martial arts. How are you supposed to protect the people you care about if you&#x27;ve never learned how? Swimming. A dangerous man is comfortable in every environment. Running. Mental toughness built one kilometer at a time. Calisthenics. How are you supposed to master anything else if you can&#x27;t even master your own body weight? Cycling. Explore the world using your legs as the engine. Free diving. Hold your breath underwater until your mind wants to quit before your body does. Spear fishing. Hunt your own food in the ocean with nothing but a spear in your lungs. Rock climbing. Problem solving with your life on the line. Dirt bike riding. Controlled aggression at speed.</details>",
