  "https://www.instagram.com/p/DcSpNEjDV0K/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>What AI Can&#x27;t Replace in Backend</b>\n<i>AI can write features in minutes but cannot replace the backend engineering depth needed to debug double-charged payments, choose database indexes, or respond to a 4 AM outage.</i>\n\n🔑 <b>Key points</b>\n• Scale breaks everything around the code, not the code itself — process, data integrity, ops\n• AI cannot explain why a payment was charged twice or diagnose a live database problem\n• Real backend expertise means knowing why a database needs an index and what to do when a service goes down at 4 AM\n\n💾 <i>Sharp framing of the gap between AI-generated code and the production-level backend judgment that keeps systems alive at scale.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DcSpNEjDV0K/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#backend #scalability #ai-limits</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>What AI Can&#x27;t Replace in Backend</b><br><i>AI can write features in minutes but cannot replace the backend engineering depth needed to debug double-charged payments, choose database indexes, or respond to a 4 AM outage.</i><br>🔑 <b>Key points</b><br><ul><li>Scale breaks everything around the code, not the code itself — process, data integrity, ops</li><li>AI cannot explain why a payment was charged twice or diagnose a live database problem</li><li>Real backend expertise means knowing why a database needs an index and what to do when a service goes down at 4 AM</li></ul><br>💾 <i>Sharp framing of the gap between AI-generated code and the production-level backend judgment that keeps systems alive at scale.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DcSpNEjDV0K/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#backend #scalability #ai-limits</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>nfactorial.school contrasts AI&#x27;s ability to write features quickly with the irreplaceable backend knowledge required to handle real production problems at scale: payment bugs, database indexing, and service outages. Calls readers to sign up for a backend scaling course.</details>",
