  "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZMAnoxuhav/": {
    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>Wrestling is the hardest sport in the world, and it&#x27;s not even close.</b>”\n— wheeler_wisdom\n\n<i>Wrestling demands more than any other sport through brutal practices, extreme early specialization, and dangerous weight cuts that eliminate athletes who didn&#x27;t start young.</i>\n💡 <b>Unlike most sports, you cannot cross over into wrestling from another discipline and succeed — the skill gap from lifelong specialists is simply unbridgeable.</b>\n\n💾 <i>Concrete case for why wrestling is uniquely demanding — useful for arguments about discipline, early specialization, and what genuine hard training looks like.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZMAnoxuhav/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#wrestling #sports #discipline</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>Wrestling is the hardest sport in the world, and it&#x27;s not even close.</b>”<br>— wheeler_wisdom<br><i>Wrestling demands more than any other sport through brutal practices, extreme early specialization, and dangerous weight cuts that eliminate athletes who didn&#x27;t start young.</i><br>💡 <b>Unlike most sports, you cannot cross over into wrestling from another discipline and succeed — the skill gap from lifelong specialists is simply unbridgeable.</b><br>💾 <i>Concrete case for why wrestling is uniquely demanding — useful for arguments about discipline, early specialization, and what genuine hard training looks like.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DZMAnoxuhav/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#wrestling #sports #discipline</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>The creator makes three arguments: practices are designed to break athletes, wrestlers must specialize from childhood with no room for crossover talent, and weight cuts of 10–15 lbs in 1–2 days are standard. Uses the NFL drafting a player with zero football experience as contrast — that would never happen in wrestling.\n\nWrestling is the hardest sport in the world, and it&#x27;s not even close. First of all, their practices are otherworldly. They typically take place in a 90-degree gym for hours of hard rolling that is literally designed to break you and weed out the weak. Not to mention, the technical proficiency of these athletes is insane. 99% of wrestlers have literally been wrestling since the day they learned to walk. You cannot come into wrestling as a great athlete somewhere else and just expect to be great day one like you could in other sports. For example, in the NFL, Uar Bernard was just drafted in the seventh round by the Eagles, and he has never played a snap of football in his life. That would never happen in wrestling. Not to mention, the weight cuts these guys have to do is borderline dangerous. They typically have to cut 10 to 15 pounds in 1 to 2 days. 10 to 15 pounds, 1 to 2 days. Yeah, there is absolutely no competition. Wrestling is the hardest sport in the world.</details>",
