              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Wrestling is the hardest sport in the world, and it's not even close. First of all, their practices are otherworldly. They typically take place in a 90-degree gym for hours of hard rolling that is literally designed to break you and weed out the weak. Not to mention, the technical proficiency of these athletes is insane. 99% of wrestlers have literally been wrestling since the day they learned to walk. You cannot come into wrestling as a great athlete somewhere else and just expect to be great day one like you could in other sports. For example, in the NFL, Uar Bernard was just drafted in the seventh round by the Eagles, and he has never played a snap of football in his life. That would never happen in wrestling. Not to mention, the weight cuts these guys have to do is borderline dangerous. They typically have to cut 10 to 15 pounds in 1 to 2 days. 10 to 15 pounds, 1 to 2 days. Yeah, there is absolutely no competition. Wrestling is the hardest sport in the world."
