            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "What did we just witness? Friday at 2 p.m. 160 runners set out on a 4.2 mile loop every hour for the last Soul Ultra. And about one hour ago on Tuesday morning in Germany, only one person remained and will be crowned champion. The mileage he ran will have you questioning absolutely everything. Throughout this race, we saw the women's world record be broken. We got to see some people run the furthest they've ever ran, and many incredible other souls take the course. But for the last 12 hours, we saw two men battle it out. Mark from the USA and Elo from Germany. There were many reports that Mark was sprinting off the start line at every loop, and making howling noises to intimidate his opponent in the middle of the night. Dog. In the end, Mark Dowdle pulled out the win, covering 395 miles or 637 kilometers over 95 loops. But Elo, who took second place, deserves all the credit for running an absolutely crazy race. Absolutely insane stuff, congrats to all of the racers, and long live the Backyard Ultra. If you love endurance sports and want to watch more stuff like this, then hit that follow button."
