    "status": "done",
    "digest": "“<b>Limits are only a figment of our imagination.</b>”\n— cam_duty\n\n<i>Three runners in Germany&#x27;s Last Soul Ultra have covered 516 km (320 miles) over more than three straight days — and are still going.</i>\n💡 <b>The human body can do things the mind refuses to believe are possible.</b>\n\n💾 <i>Raw proof that human endurance limits are almost entirely self-imposed — 320 miles in 3+ days with runners still upright.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcJjwDQiflX/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#ultramarathon #endurance #human-limits</i>",
    "markdown": "“<b>Limits are only a figment of our imagination.</b>”<br>— cam_duty<br><i>Three runners in Germany&#x27;s Last Soul Ultra have covered 516 km (320 miles) over more than three straight days — and are still going.</i><br>💡 <b>The human body can do things the mind refuses to believe are possible.</b><br>💾 <i>Raw proof that human endurance limits are almost entirely self-imposed — 320 miles in 3+ days with runners still upright.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcJjwDQiflX/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#ultramarathon #endurance #human-limits</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>Cam Duty covers the live Last Soul Ultra race in Germany where three runners have surpassed 320 miles over more than three days with no end in sight — framed as proof that human physical limits are far beyond what we imagine.\n\nI can&#x27;t believe what&#x27;s happening in Germany right now. They started this race on Friday at 2pm and it is now Monday at 7pm and they are still going. What the hell? Yesterday I made a video about the last Seoul Ultra race and there were 7 runners remaining at the time. Well, new update. There are now 3 runners remaining and the mileage is absolutely unbelievable. I literally can&#x27;t believe it. The 3 remaining absolute savages are Norman, Mark, and Ayu. Please forgive me if I mispronounce that. And honestly, I don&#x27;t know how, but they still look pretty damn good. This is a video from the live stream if you want to check it out. And here&#x27;s the crazy part. They have covered 516 kilometers or 320 miles. Anyways, if you needed some Monday motivation, let this be it. This is a testimony to how insane the human body is and that limits are only a figment of our imagination. I have no idea how long this is going to go, but I know this ending is going to be epic.</details>",
