              "text": "I can't believe what's happening in Germany right now. They started this race on Friday at 2pm and it is now Monday at 7pm and they are still going. What the hell? Yesterday I made a video about the last Seoul Ultra race and there were 7 runners remaining at the time. Well, new update. There are now 3 runners remaining and the mileage is absolutely unbelievable. I literally can't believe it. The 3 remaining absolute savages are Norman, Mark, and Ayu. Please forgive me if I mispronounce that. And honestly, I don't know how, but they still look pretty damn good. This is a video from the live stream if you want to check it out. And here's the crazy part. They have covered 516 kilometers or 320 miles. Anyways, if you needed some Monday motivation, let this be it. This is a testimony to how insane the human body is and that limits are only a figment of our imagination. I have no idea how long this is going to go, but I know this ending is going to be epic."
