or supplement companies. Next up, we have Claire. Which is a wearable for women&#x27;s hormone health. Health brands are doubling down on the women&#x27;s market because they take up 80% of the spending. Claire Health captures this demand with wearables that give insights beyond generic data. It identifies patterns for cycle changes and symptoms, training and recovery flows for energy optimization, and even data-driven insights around fertility planning. So you can win in this market if you provide a solution that removes friction and creates a tangible outcome. Next up, we have Rhythm. This is an at-home blood test that became widely available in 2026. Their test tracks over 25 biomarkers, including hormones, metabolic efficiency, biological age, and many more. Then the results sync through to an app which gives you AI-powered insights and actionable steps to achieve your health goals. The pattern amongst all the latest innovations is they prioritize removing friction because people don&#x27;t want to add to their routine. They want to integrate. And the brands leading the industry have this at the center of their strategy. If you want a full breakdown of the fastest-growing brands with the best innovations, comment Innovate below and I&#x27;ll send it through.</details>",
