    "status": "done",
    "digest": "<b>3 Storytelling Resources to Start</b>\n\n📌 <b>Recommended</b>\n⚠️ The Neuroscience of Addictive Storytelling — Polly Way (phonetic: &#x27;Pallyway&#x27; in transcript — channel name unconfirmed) — <i>Transcript renders creator name phonetically as &#x27;Pallyway&#x27;; could not search to confirm channel name or video URL. Search on YouTube for the title to find the correct video.</i>\n⚠️ Only Three Ingredients to Become a Better Storyteller — Vin Yang (phonetic: &#x27;Vinnyang&#x27; in transcript — channel name unconfirmed) — <i>Transcript renders creator name phonetically as &#x27;Vinnyang&#x27;; could not search to confirm channel name or video URL. Search on YouTube for the title to find the correct video.</i>\n⚠️ The Science of Storytelling — Will Storr (transcript mishears as &#x27;Will Stahl&#x27;) — <i>Almost certainly Will Storr&#x27;s 2019 book on how the brain processes narrative — a well-known title — but search was unavailable to confirm the canonical Goodreads/publisher link. Verify at goodreads.com.</i>\n\n💾 <i>A curated starter kit of two YouTube videos and one book for learning storytelling from a neuroscience and psychology angle, useful for building business content.</i>\n🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbs4HcUhc9p/\">Original reel</a>\n<i>#storytelling #content-creation #resources</i>",
    "markdown": "<b>3 Storytelling Resources to Start</b><br>📌 <b>Recommended</b><br><ol><li>⚠️ The Neuroscience of Addictive Storytelling — Polly Way (phonetic: &#x27;Pallyway&#x27; in transcript — channel name unconfirmed) — <i>Transcript renders creator name phonetically as &#x27;Pallyway&#x27;; could not search to confirm channel name or video URL. Search on YouTube for the title to find the correct video.</i></li><li>⚠️ Only Three Ingredients to Become a Better Storyteller — Vin Yang (phonetic: &#x27;Vinnyang&#x27; in transcript — channel name unconfirmed) — <i>Transcript renders creator name phonetically as &#x27;Vinnyang&#x27;; could not search to confirm channel name or video URL. Search on YouTube for the title to find the correct video.</i></li><li>⚠️ The Science of Storytelling — Will Storr (transcript mishears as &#x27;Will Stahl&#x27;) — <i>Almost certainly Will Storr&#x27;s 2019 book on how the brain processes narrative — a well-known title — but search was unavailable to confirm the canonical Goodreads/publisher link. Verify at goodreads.com.</i></li></ol><br>💾 <i>A curated starter kit of two YouTube videos and one book for learning storytelling from a neuroscience and psychology angle, useful for building business content.</i><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbs4HcUhc9p/\">Original reel</a><br><i>#storytelling #content-creation #resources</i><details><summary>📄 Full transcript</summary>A starter resource list for content creators who want to understand storytelling at the principles level — neuroscience of why people can&#x27;t look away, the essential building blocks of story structure, and the psychology of narrative from Will Storr&#x27;s book.\n\nThis is actually how you develop God-given storytelling research that&#x27;s actually going to help you grow your business through content. This is episode one of StoryMaxing. Watch the neuroscience of addictive storytelling by Pallyway. It will rewire how you think about why people can&#x27;t look away from certain stories. Now obviously one video is not going to make you a better storyteller. You could also watch Only Three Ingredients to Become a Better Storyteller by Vinnyang. He breaks down the exact building blocks every story needs. Then read The Science of Storytelling by Will Stahl. It breaks down why our brains are literally wired for narratives. I can&#x27;t fit all my resources into one video. Comment lists and I&#x27;ll send a full one to you to start your storytelling journey.</details>",
